ing":null,"first":"Luise Holberg","key":"lindgrenpau","last":"Lindgren","name":"Lindgren, Luise Holberg","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tanja","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","name":"Thomsen, Tanja","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Merete Lund","key":"hetlandpau","last":"Hetland","locid":"3407b4a7-174d-43db-bae6-74e7f035a81f","name":"Hetland, Merete Lund","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Mette","key":"aadahlpau","last":"Aadahl","locid":"019b268b-8dff-4a10-91f6-07730c29d39b","name":"Aadahl, Mette","orcid":"0000-0001-5904-9747","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Sara Danshøj","key":"kristensenpau","last":"Kristensen","name":"Kristensen, Sara Danshøj","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Annette","key":"dethurahpau","last":"de Thurah","locid":"6429fc0a-b979-4ddb-ac99-3214574a17af","name":"de Thurah, Annette","orcid":"0000-0003-0103-4328","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Bente Appel","key":"esbensenpau","last":"Esbensen","locid":"36196dc3-ccaa-4877-aab9-b3ebbc3869b1","name":"Esbensen, Bente Appel","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39934926"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s40814-025-01601-z","issn":["20555784"],"issue":"1","journal":"Pilot and Feasibility Studies","paperid":"15","publisher":"BioMed Central","status":"p","title":"Pilot and Feasibility Studies","volume":"11"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85218629495"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-1e9d4e5a-e343-49e7-b6d6-1eaa71cf17f1","ku-08959186-f843-4909-b7cf-3fc4d338742e"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A self-management intervention for newly diagnosed with inflammatory arthritis : a randomized controlled feasibility and fidelity study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-793167","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Patients with the genetic disorder Niemann-Pick type C2 disease (NP-C2) suffer from lysosomal accumulation of cholesterol causing both systemic and severe neurological symptoms. In a murine NP-C2 model, otherwise successful intravenous Niemann-Pick C2 protein (NPC2) replacement therapy fails to alleviate progressive neurodegeneration as infused NPC2 cannot cross the blood-brain barrier (BBB). Genetic modification of brain endothelial cells (BECs) is thought to enable secretion of recombinant proteins thereby overcoming the restrictions of the BBB. We hypothesized that an adeno-associated virus (AAV-BR1) encoding the Npc2 gene could cure neurological symptoms in Npc2-/- mice through transduction of BECs, and possibly neurons via viral passage across the BBB. METHODS: Six weeks old Npc2-/- mice were intravenously injected with the AAV-BR1-NPC2 vector. Composite phenotype scores and behavioral tests were assessed for the following 6 weeks and visually documented. Post-mortem analyses included gene expression analyses, verification of neurodegeneration in Purkinje cells, determination of NPC2 transduction in the CNS, assessment of gliosis, quantification of gangliosides, and co-detection of cholesterol with NPC2 in degenerating neurons. RESULTS: Treatment with the AAV-BR1-NPC2 vector improved motor functions, reduced neocortical inflammation, and preserved Purkinje cells in most of the mice, referred to as high responders. The vector exerted tropism for BECs and neurons resulting in a widespread NPC2 distribution in the brain with a concomitant reduction of cholesterol in adjacent neurons, presumably not transduced by the vector. Mass spectrometry imaging revealed distinct lipid alterations in the brains of Npc2-/- mice, with increased GM2 and GM3 ganglioside accumulation in the cerebellum and hippocampus. AAV-BR1-NPC2 treatment partially normalized these ganglioside distributions in high responders, including restoration of lipid profiles towards those of Npc2+/+ controls. CONCLUSION: The data suggests cross-correcting gene therapy to the brain via delivery of NPC2 from BECs and neurons.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Charlotte Laurfelt Munch","Frederiksen, Signe Frost","Heegaard, Christian Würtz","Thomsen, Maj Schneider","Hede, Eva","Laczek, Bartosz","Körbelin, Jakob","Wüstner, Daniel","Thomsen, Louiza Bohn","Schwaninger, Markus","Jensen, Ole N","Moos, Torben","Burkhart, Annette"],"cuid":["S03-100.00-792938"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Burkhart, Annette","Moos, Torben"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University Medical Center Hamburg-Eppendorf","University of Hamburg","University of Lübeck"],"keyword":["AAV BR1","Animals","Blood brain barrier","Brain metabolism","Cholesterol","Cross correction","Dependovirus genetics","Disease Models Animal","Endothelial Cells metabolism","Gangliosides","Genetic Therapy methods","Mice","Mice Knockout","NPC2","Neurons metabolism","Niemann Pick Disease Type C therapy","Niemann Pick type C2 disease","Vesicular Transport Proteins","Viral gene therapy"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"endothelial and neuronal engagement by aav br000000000001 gene therapy alleviates neurological symptoms and lipid deposition in a mouse model of niemann pick type c000000000002","src":["aau","au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12987-025-00621-4","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This work was funded by Fonden til Lægevidenskabens Fremme, Direktør Emil C. Hertz og hustru Inger Hertz' Fond, Dagmar Marshalls Fond, Lundbeck Foundation ((Research Initiative on Blood–Brain Barriers and Drug Delivery Grant no. 2013-14113), and Grant no. R366-2021-226), Hørslev-Fonden, Læge Sophus Carl Emil Friis og Hustru Olga Doris Friis Legat, Scleroseforeningen (Grant no. A41926), the Danish Research Council (Grant no. 2024-00136B), and Svend Andersen Fonden as well as the German Research Foundation (DFG, SFB1328-A13, Grant no. 335447717). The Biological Mass Spectrometry Research at SDU is supported by a generous grant from the Novo Nordisk Foundation (grant no. NNF20OC0061575 to O.N.J.) to establish mass spectrometry imaging technology as part of the INTEGRA research infrastructure. The authors thank laboratory technicians Merete Fredsgaard, Hanne Krone Nielsen, Ditte Bech Laursen, and Louise Hvilshøj Madsen, Aalborg University, Denmark, and animal technicians Karina Lassen Holm and Dorte Hermansen, Aarhus University, Denmark, for excellent technical assistance during the study. Associate Professor Anders Olsen and Helene Halkjær Jensen, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience, Aalborg University are acknowledged for assistance with the use of the Olympus IX83 inverted microscope equipped with Yokogawa confocal CSU-W1 spinning disk."],"id":"S03-100.00-792938","identifier":[{"id":"39891227","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85217442531","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC11786545","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["aau-87ba764f-e6be-49ac-af3c-235def6f972b","au-c7024848-3bf8-4c4f-9bb4-d0689830c925","sdu-82fa5766-cd5c-45ef-b638-689440f77fd9"],"keyword":["AAV-BR1","Animals","Blood–brain barrier","Brain/metabolism","Cholesterol","Cross-correction","Dependovirus/genetics","Disease Models, Animal","Endothelial Cells/metabolism","Gangliosides","Genetic Therapy/methods","Genetic Vectors/administration & dosage","Mice","Mice, Knockout","NPC2","Neurons/metabolism","Niemann-Pick Disease, Type C/therapy","Niemann-Pick type C2 disease","Vesicular Transport Proteins","Viral gene therapy"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-BFB0D886862379C8525CCF6FA4418521"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/284127702/s12987-025-00621-4.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12987-025-00621-4","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/765010669/s12987-025-00621-4.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, Neurobiology Research and Drug Delivery"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Biochemistry and Molecular Biology","SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Biochemistry and Molecular Biology, Biomedical Mass Spectrometry and Systems Biology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Molecular Biology and Genetics, Department of Molecular Biology and Genetics - Cellular Health, Intervention, and Nutrition"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"de","key":"university medical center hamburg eppendorf","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University Medical Center Hamburg-Eppendorf","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"de","key":"university of hamburg","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Hamburg","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"de","key":"university of lübeck","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Lübeck","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Charlotte Laurfelt Munch","key":"rasmussencharlottelaurfeltmunchpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"608faa0d-42e3-46c7-bbeb-95118471e801","name":"Rasmussen, Charlotte Laurfelt Munch","orcid":"0000-0001-6535-3729","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Signe Frost","key":"frederiksensignefrostpau","last":"Frederiksen","locid":"7f13073c-fee5-4809-ba79-17e080e376e0","name":"Frederiksen, Signe Frost","orcid":"0009-0001-5288-3349","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christian Würtz","key":"heegaardchristianwürtzpau","last":"Heegaard","locid":"f7804b8e-023c-4aab-8102-0a1d95b20760","name":"Heegaard, Christian Würtz","orcid":"0000-0002-7989-2624","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Maj Schneider","key":"thomsenmajschneiderpau","last":"Thomsen","locid":"500ff43a-765e-4d61-9bbd-f228196ed49d","name":"Thomsen, Maj Schneider","orcid":"0000-0002-8385-7039","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Eva","key":"hedeevapau","last":"Hede","locid":"31fc1c6e-3bbd-4494-9b40-f66d601bed36","name":"Hede, Eva","orcid":"0000-0002-6072-4970","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","f