{"abstract":"Motivation: INCA is a powerful tool for metabolic flux analysis, however, import and export of data and results can be tedious and limit the use of INCA in automated workflows. Results: The INCAWrapper enables the use of INCA purely through Python, which allows the use of INCA in common data science workflows.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Mattanovich, Matthias","Hesselberg-Thomsen, Viktor","Lien, Annette","Vaitkus, Dovydas","Saad, Victoria Sara","McCloskey, Douglas"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-768147"],"filters":{"added":"2024-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Hesselberg-Thomsen, Viktor","Mattanovich, Matthias"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","BioMed X"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"incawrapper a python wrapper for inca for seamless data import export and processing","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/bioadv/vbae100","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This work was supported by the Novo Nordisk Foundation [NNF19CC0035454 to M.M. and NNF14OC0009473 to V.H.T.]."],"id":"S02-100.00-768147","identifier":[{"id":"PMC11245311","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85198924784","type":"scopus"},{"id":"39006966","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-11f32d2e-0d00-47eb-b075-6656211650f2","ku-36dcb29d-42d8-4142-9955-eca88b478074"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-BB5DB7A8BEB81F2EE5D216943D1910ED"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/380091370/vbae100.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/399748805/vbae100.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/bioadv/vbae100","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Novo Nordisk Foundation Center for Basic Metabolic Research, Moritz Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","country":"dk","first":"Matthias","key":"mattanovichpau","last":"Mattanovich","locid":"67fc21b3-1868-4100-bd04-fd100bd0ef16","name":"Mattanovich, Matthias","orcid":"0000-0001-7561-7898","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Viktor","key":"hesselbergthomsenpau","last":"Hesselberg-Thomsen","locid":"4fc30293-13e7-486d-aa39-c1e9de21f918","name":"Hesselberg-Thomsen, Viktor","orcid":"0000-0001-6929-3671","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Annette","key":"lienpau","last":"Lien","name":"Lien, Annette","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Dovydas","key":"vaitkuspau","last":"Vaitkus","locid":"49ee293b-d234-4ac4-ad5d-d66fbd57c811","name":"Vaitkus, Dovydas","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Victoria Sara","key":"saadpau","last":"Saad","name":"Saad, Victoria Sara","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Douglas","key":"mccloskeypau","last":"McCloskey","locid":"93f43df0-ccbf-411a-ac74-0568fd602f36","name":"McCloskey, Douglas","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39006966"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/bioadv/vbae100","issn":["26350041"],"issue":"1","journal":"Bioinformatics Advances","paperid":"vbae100","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"Bioinformatics Advances","volume":"4"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85198924784"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-11f32d2e-0d00-47eb-b075-6656211650f2","ku-36dcb29d-42d8-4142-9955-eca88b478074"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"INCAWrapper : a Python wrapper for INCA for seamless data import, -export, and -processing","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-768147","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"The N-methyl-d-aspartate (NMDA) receptor is a glutamate-activated cation channel that is critical to many processes in the brain. Genome-wide association studies suggest that glutamatergic neurotransmission and NMDA receptor-mediated synaptic plasticity are important for body weight homeostasis1. Here we report the engineering and preclinical development of a bimodal molecule that integrates NMDA receptor antagonism with glucagon-like peptide-1 (GLP-1) receptor agonism to effectively reverse obesity, hyperglycaemia and dyslipidaemia in rodent models of metabolic disease. GLP-1-directed delivery of the NMDA receptor antagonist MK-801 affects neuroplasticity in the hypothalamus and brainstem. Importantly, targeting of MK-801 to GLP-1 receptor-expressing brain regions circumvents adverse physiological and behavioural effects associated with MK-801 monotherapy. In summary, our approach demonstrates the feasibility of using peptide-mediated targeting to achieve cell-specific ionotropic receptor modulation and highlights the therapeutic potential of unimolecular mixed GLP-1 receptor agonism and NMDA receptor antagonism for safe and effective obesity treatment.","author_count":33,"contributors":["Petersen, Jonas","Ludwig, Mette Q.","Juozaityte, Vaida","Ranea-Robles, Pablo","Svendsen, Charlotte","Hwang, Eunsang","Kristensen, Amalie W.","Fadahunsi, Nicole","Lund, Jens","Breum, Alberte Wollesen","Mathiesen, Cecilie Vad","Sachs, Luisa","Moreno-Justicia, Roger","Rohlfs, Rebecca","Ford, James C.","Douros, Jonathan D.","Finan, Brian","Portillo, Bryan","Grose, Kyle","Petersen, Jacob E.","Trauelsen, Mette","Feuchtinger, Annette","DiMarchi, Richard D.","Schwartz, Thue W.","Deshmukh, Atul S.","Thomsen, Morten B.","Kohlmeier, Kristi Anne","Williams, Kevin W.","Pers, Tune H.","Frølund, Bente","Strømgaard, Kristian","Klein, Anders Bue","Clemmensen, Christoffer"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-747908"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Helmholtz Centre Munich","Indiana University Bloomington","University of Texas Southwestern Medical Center"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-NOVO"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-NOVO","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"glp 000000000001 directed nmda receptor antagonism for obesity treatment","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-024-07419-8","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-747908","identifier":[{"id":"38750368","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC11136670","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85192940391","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-40efbbda-b63d-4d00-a731-45075e427939"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-69B7CB7C2E1977C77659720953AB8652"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-024-07419-8","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/393264760/s41586_024_07419_8.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Drug Design and Pharmacology, Medicinal Chemistry","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Novo Nordisk Foundation Center for Basic Metabolic Research, Clemmensen Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"