"key":"søndergaardpau","last":"Søndergaard","name":"Søndergaard, Helle B.","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37337838"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/ene.15930","issn":["13515101","14681331"],"issn_org":["13515101"],"issue":"10","journal":"European Journal of Neurology","pages":"3212-3220","status":"p","title":"European Journal of Neurology","volume":"30"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85164500287"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-7dc29d52-0fa5-406f-bbd1-2599fac9ca4e"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The peripheral endocannabinoid system and its association with biomarkers of inflammation in untreated patients with multiple sclerosis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-695994","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"INTRODUCTION: The treatment of neurological diseases is significantly hampered by the lack of available therapeutics. A major restraint for the development of drugs is denoted by the presence of the blood-brain barrier (BBB), which precludes the transfer of biotherapeutics to the brain due to size restraints. AREAS COVERED: Novel optimism for transfer of biotherapeutics to the brain has been generated via development of targeted therapeutics to nutrient transporters expressed by brain capillary endothelial cells (BCECs). Targeting approaches with antibodies acting as biological drug carriers allow for proteins and genetic material to enter the brain, and qualified therapy using targeted proteins for protein replacement has been observed in preclinical models and now emerging in the clinic. Viral vectors denote an alternative for protein delivery to the brain by uptake and transduction of BCECs, or by transport through the BBB leading to neuronal transduction. EXPERT OPINION: The breaching of the BBB to large molecules has opened for treatment of diseases in the brain. A sturdier understanding of how biotherapeutics undergo transport through the BBB and how successful transport into the brain can be monitored is required to further improve the translation from successful preclinical studies to the clinic.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Moos, Torben","Thomsen, Maj Schneider","Burkhart, Annette","Hede, Eva","Laczek, Bartosz"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-705725"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Moos, Torben"],"keyword":["Antibody","Blood brain barrier","Nanobody","Targeting","Transferrin receptor","Viral gene therapy"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"targeted transport of biotherapeutics at the blood brain barrier","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"djr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85180258333&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Some of the most recent results obtained and described by the authors were generated by generous grants from the Danish Research Council (Grant no. 1030-00474B), the Lundbeck Foundation Research Initiative on Brain Barriers and Drug Delivery (Grant no. R155-2013-14113), and Scleroseforeningen [Grant no. A41926]."],"id":"S01-000.00-705725","identifier":[{"id":"38059358","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85180258333","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-a4889f57-e1f7-4e79-b8a2-1d581f0aa041"],"keyword":["Antibody","CD98","blood-brain barrier","brain capillary endothelial cell","nanobody","targeting","transferrin receptor","viral gene therapy"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-678FDD789A37B7ECBEB7AC8D9779CA2E"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, Neurobiology Research and Drug Delivery","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Neuroboost"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Torben","key":"moospau","last":"Moos","locid":"e51cbd29-97d2-42d8-bbca-11f026378a2f","name":"Moos, Torben","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Schneider","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","locid":"500ff43a-765e-4d61-9bbd-f228196ed49d","name":"Thomsen, Maj Schneider","name_org":"Thomsen, Schneider","orcid":"0000-0002-8385-7039","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Annette","key":"burkhartpau","last":"Burkhart","locid":"7b6bd909-a011-463c-9e09-3623fee043b3","name":"Burkhart, Annette","orcid":"0000-0003-2086-4693","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Eva","key":"hedepau","last":"Hede","locid":"31fc1c6e-3bbd-4494-9b40-f66d601bed36","name":"Hede, Eva","orcid":"0000-0002-6072-4970","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Bartosz","key":"laczekpau","last":"Laczek","locid":"f7fe37c1-531e-45bc-8e1b-044993b493f3","name":"Laczek, Bartosz","orcid":"0000-0002-5209-9562","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38059358"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/17425247.2023.2292697","issn":["17425247","17447593"],"issn_org":["17425247"],"issue":"12","journal":"Expert Opinion on Drug Delivery","pages":"1823-1838","publisher":"Taylor & Francis","status":"p","title":"Expert Opinion on Drug Delivery","volume":"20"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85180258333"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-a4889f57-e1f7-4e79-b8a2-1d581f0aa041"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Targeted transport of biotherapeutics at the blood-brain barrier","type":"Journal Review","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-705725","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"INTRODUCTION: Niemann-Pick type C2 disease (NP-C2) is a fatal neurovisceral disorder caused by defects in the lysosomal cholesterol transporter protein NPC2. Consequently, cholesterol and other lipids accumulate within the lysosomes, causing a heterogeneous spectrum of clinical manifestations. Murine models are essential for increasing the understanding of the complex pathology of NP-C2. This study, therefore, aims to describe the neurovisceral pathology in the NPC2-deficient mouse model to evaluate its correlation to human NP-C2. METHODS: Npc2-/- mice holding the LST105 mutation were used in the present study (Npc2Gt(LST105)BygNya). Body and organ weight and histopathological evaluations were carried out in six and 12-week-old Npc2-/- mice, with a special emphasis on neuropathology. The Purkinje cell (PC) marker calbindin, the astrocytic marker GFAP, and the microglia marker IBA1 were included to assess PC degeneration and neuroinflammation, respectively. In addition, the pathology of the liver, lungs, and spleen was assessed using hematoxylin and eosin staining. RESULTS: Six weeks old pre-symptomatic Npc2-/- mice showed splenomegaly and obvious neuropathological changes, especially in the cerebellum, where initial PC loss and neuroinflammation were evident. The Npc2-/- mice developed neurological symptoms at eight weeks of age, severely progressing until the end-stage of the disease at 12 weeks. At the end-stage of the disease, Npc2-/- mice were characterized by growth retardation, tremor, cerebellar ataxia, splenomegaly, foam cell accumulation in the lungs, liver, and spleen, brain atrophy, pronounced PC degeneration, and severe neuroinflammation. CONCLUSION: The Npc2Gt(LST105)BygNya mouse model resembles the pathology seen in NP-C2 patients and denotes a valuable model for increasing the understanding of the complex disease manifestation and is relevant for testing the efficacies of new treatment strategies.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Charlotte Laurfelt Munch","Thomsen, Louiza Bohn","Heegaard, Christian Würtz","Moos, Torben","Burkhart, Annette"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-681275"],"filters":{"added":"2023-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Burkhart, Annette"],"keyword":["Cerebellar Purkinje cell","Mouse models","NPC2","Neurodegeneration","Niemann Pick type C2 disease"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the npc000000000002 sup gt lst000000000105 bygnya sup mouse signifies pathological changes comparable to human niemann pick type c000000000002 disease","src":["aau","au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.mcn.2023.103880","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-681275","identifier":[{"id":"37454976","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85165236188","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-9501f66c-5519-47ec-a0bd-92e31e613669","au-625eb9c0-9854-4373-9666-fc0c6f3fa545"],"keyword":["Cerebellar Purkinje cell","Mouse models","NPC2","Neurodegeneration","Niemann-Pick type C2 disease"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-23B300ABD2DC7AB980663DCC692EC810"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/417993880/1-s2.0-S104474312300074X-main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/753136105/1-s2.0-S104474312300074X-main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.mcn.2023.103880","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, Neurobiology Research and Drug Delivery"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Molecular Biology and Genetics, Department of Molecular Biology and Genetics - Cellular Health, Intervention, and Nutrition"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Charlotte Laurfelt Munch","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"608faa0d-42e3-46c7-bbeb-95118471e801","name":"Rasmussen, Charlotte Laurfelt Munch","orcid":"0000-0001-6535-3729","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Louiza Bohn","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","locid":"c4698d51-553a-4391-90b0-5379982b935f","name":"Thomsen, Louiza Bohn","orcid":"0000-0002-3144-7150","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christian Würtz","key":"heegaardpau","last":"Heegaard","locid":"f7804b8e-023c-4aab-8102-0a1d95b20760","name":"Heegaard, Christian Würtz","orcid":"0000-0002-7989-2624","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Torben","key":"moospau","last":"Moos","locid":"e51cbd29-97d2-42d8-bbca-11f026378a2f","name":"Moos, Torben","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Annette","key":"burkhartpau","last":"Burkhart","locid":"7b6bd909-a011-463c-9e09-3623fee043b3","name":"Burkhart, Annette","orcid":"0000-0003-2086-4693","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37454976"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.mcn.2023.103880","issn":["10447431","10959327"],"issn_org":["10447431"],"journal":"Molecular and Cellular Neuroscience","paperid":"103880","publisher":"Academic Press Inc.","status":"p","title":"Molecular and Cellular Neuroscience","volume":"126"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85165236188"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-9501f66c-5519-47ec-a0bd-92e31e613669","au-625eb9c0-9854-4373-9666-fc0c6f3fa545"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University"],"title":"The Npc2Gt(LST105)BygNya mouse signifies pathological changes comparable to human Niemann-Pick type C2 disease","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-681275","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"This report presents scenarios for future (2030) land-use in agriculture & forestry, and for exploitation of marine resources. The newest knowledge on resource efficient production methods (e.g., maximal carbon capture by photosynthesis & efficient nutrient use) have been used to frame the three scenarios: Business-as-usual mimicking a continuation of the current conditions for production of biomass. Biomass assuming sustainable intensification of the production. Extensification taking into account significant environment, climate and nature concerns. For agriculture, also the effects of +/- 20 % animal production are analysed. The scenarios resulted in increased biomass delivery of up to 13 M tonnes of dry matter for agriculture. No significant increase was found in forestry delivery by 2030 due to the sectors’ long production cycles. Marine biomass contributed up to 58 ktonnes of dry matter. Integrated biorefinery systems were set up for analysing cascade utilization of the biomass and budget economics are discussed. The scenarios have large impacts on the land-use with up to 11 % of the farmed area set aside for nature purposes in Extensification, and with significant reductions in greenhouse gas emissions and nitrate leaching in all scenarios.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Gylling, Morten","Nord-Larsen, Thomas","Bruhn, Annette","Thomsen, Marianne","Ambye-Jensen, Morten","Mortensen, Esben Øster","Jørgensen, Uffe"],"cuid":["S02-084.38-698064"],"filters":{"added":"2023-09","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["T0 2023"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"potential danish biomass production and utilization in 000000002030","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/335673969/DCA_Rapport_0823.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-084.38-698064","ids":["au-f014eca9-2aab-434f-832d-bb35fd42571e","ku-f960a1eb-bf86-417c-a3bb-2e7e2ba9b152"],"keyword":["T0-2023","TO-23"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-2-7EC23C2F74651E58248132580BECFED2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/335673969/DCA_Rapport_0823.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://dcapub.au.dk/djfpublikation/djfpdf/DCArapport219.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/373616325/DCArapport219.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Food and Resource Economics, Section for Production, Markets and Policy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Ecoscience, Department of Ecoscience - Marine Ecology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Morten","key":"gyllingpau","last":"Gylling","locid":"27d0d73f-eca6-4385-bc2d-6eb3a1ae8fcd","name":"Gylling, Morten","orcid":"0000-0002-2792-5527","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Thomas","key":"nordlarsenpau","last":"Nord-Larsen","locid":"d5b3bda9-5a06-45e4-8c9a-07e768bef87a","name":"Nord-Larsen, Thomas","orcid":"0000-0002-5341-6435","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Annette","key":"bruhnpau","last":"Bruhn","locid":"15559017-3036-4e04-968e-338a24d800ce","name":"Bruhn, Annette","orcid":"0000-0002-7940-1338","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Marianne","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","locid":"a829b47d-f5d2-404d-b768-ec12fbb3b661","name":"Thomsen, Marianne","orcid":"0000-0003-2453-5141","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Morten","key":"ambyejensenpau","last":"Ambye-Jensen","locid":"9f74b922-bac9-44db-b3a3-31c9b450ebe8","name":"Ambye-Jensen, Morten","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Esben Øster","key":"mortensenpau","last":"Mortensen","locid":"641b5037-264c-46a0-8ecf-1d0a8dd74f27","name":"Mortensen, Esben Øster","orcid":"0000-0002-4890-9593","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Uffe","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"efa7e924-c197-4060-8904-110cf0a30837","name":"Jørgensen, Uffe","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788794420211."],"issn":["22451684"],"issue":"219","pages":"82","publisher":"DCA - Nationalt Center for Fødevarer og Jordbrug","repno":"DCA Report, No. 219","series":"DCA Report","status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-f014eca9-2aab-434f-832d-bb35fd42571e","ku-f960a1eb-bf86-417c-a3bb-2e7e2ba9b152"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Potential Danish biomass production and utilization in 2030","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-084.38-698064","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Treating central nervous system (CNS) diseases is complicated by the incapability of numerous therapeutics to cross the blood–brain barrier (BBB), mainly composed of brain endothelial cells (BECs). Genetically modifying BECs into protein factories that supply the CNS with recombinant proteins is a promising approach to overcome this hindrance, especially in genetic diseases, like Niemann Pick disease type C2 (NPC2), where both CNS and peripheral cells are affected. Here, we investigated the potential of the BEC-specific adeno-associated viral vector (AAV-BR1) encoding NPC2 for expression and secretion from primary BECs cultured in an in vitro BBB model with mixed glial cells, and in healthy BALB/c mice. Transduced primary BECs had significantly increased NPC2 gene expression and secreted NPC2 after viral transduction, which significantly reversed cholesterol deposition in NPC2 deficient fibroblasts. Mice receiving an intravenous injection with AAV-BR1-NCP2-eGFP were sacrificed 8 weeks later and examined for its biodistribution and transgene expression of eGFP and NPC2. AAV-BR1-NPC2-eGFP was distributed mainly to the brain and lightly to the heart and lung, but did not label other organs including the liver. eGFP expression was primarily found in BECs throughout the brain but occasionally also in neurons suggesting transport of the vector across the BBB, a phenomenon also confirmed in vitro. NPC2 gene expression was up-regulated in the brain, and recombinant NPC2 protein expression was observed in both transduced brain capillaries and neurons. Our findings show that AAV-BR1 transduction of BECs is possible and that it may denote a promising strategy for future treatment of NPC2. (Figure presented.)","author_count":9,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Charlotte Laurfelt Munch","Hede, Eva","Routhe, Lisa Juul","Körbelin, Jakob","Helgudottir, Steinunn Sara","Thomsen, Louiza Bohn","Schwaninger, Markus","Burkhart, Annette","Moos, Torben"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-092686"],"filters":{"added":"2022-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Burkhart, Annette","Moos, Torben"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University Medical Center Hamburg-Eppendorf","University of Lübeck"],"keyword":["AAV BR1","Blood brain barrier","Niemann Pick disease type C2","Viral gene therapy"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a novel strategy for delivering niemann pick type c000000000002 proteins across the blood brain barrier using the brain endothelial specific aav br000000000001 virus","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/jnc.15621","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The authors thank the laboratory technicians Hanne Krone Nielsen, Merete Fredsgaard, and Louise Hvilshøj Madsen, and the animal technicians at the animal facility at Aalborg University, Denmark for excellent technical assistance throughout the study. We thank Martin Trepel, University Medical Center Augsburg, Germany, for supervising the initial development of the BEC‐targeted AAV‐BR1 mutant. We thank Maj Schneider Thomsen for the illustration of the BBB model. This work was funded by generous grants from the Research Initiative on Blood–Brain Barrier and Drug Delivery (RIBBDD) founded by the Lundbeck Foundation (grant no: 2013‐14113), Svend Andersen Fonden, Læge Sophus Carl Emil Friis og Hustru Olga Doris Friis Legat, Hørslev Fonden, Civilingeniør Frode V. Nyegaard og Hustrus Fond, Fonden for Lægevidenskabens Fremme, Torben og Alice Frimodts Fond, Oda og Hans Svenningsens Fond, and Kong Christian d. X fond. in vitro The authors thank the laboratory technicians Hanne Krone Nielsen, Merete Fredsgaard, and Louise Hvilshøj Madsen, and the animal technicians at the animal facility at Aalborg University, Denmark for excellent technical assistance throughout the study. We thank Martin Trepel, University Medical Center Augsburg, Germany, for supervising the initial development of the BEC-targeted AAV-BR1 mutant. We thank Maj Schneider Thomsen for the illustration of the in vitro BBB model. This work was funded by generous grants from the Research Initiative on Blood–Brain Barrier and Drug Delivery (RIBBDD) founded by the Lundbeck Foundation (grant no: 2013-14113), Svend Andersen Fonden, Læge Sophus Carl Emil Friis og Hustru Olga Doris Friis Legat, Hørslev Fonden, Civilingeniør Frode V. Nyegaard og Hustrus Fond, Fonden for Lægevidenskabens Fremme, Torben og Alice Frimodts Fond, Oda og Hans Svenningsens Fond, and Kong Christian d. X fond."],"id":"S01-000.00-092686","identifier":[{"id":"85130558332","type":"scopus"},{"id":"35554935","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-92d8a9c4-0a20-4ac1-b254-b2189e96e900"],"keyword":["AAV-BR1","AAV2","Niemann Pick disease type C2","blood–brain barrier","viral gene therapy"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-620C62CB137C7C7928C642FD746DD13E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/jnc.15621","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/526728861/Journal_of_Neurochemistry_2022_Rasmussen_A_novel_strategy_for_delivering_Niemann_Pick_type_C2_proteins_across_the.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty