i Bhagya","key":"samarasinghemilanibhagyapau","last":"Samarasinghe","locid":"b52c1f00-daeb-4d9b-b2f9-c47288e056db","name":"Samarasinghe, Milani Bhagya","orcid":"0000-0003-4946-1150","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Élisabeth","key":"chasséélisabethpau","last":"Chassé","locid":"3e64d39c-a457-4f42-a066-e4f9a7ffad99","name":"Chassé, Élisabeth","orcid":"0000-0002-8651-4971","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","first":"Cecilie Heide","key":"nielsencecilieheidepau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"2c74421b-1780-45ad-a6b2-85fbf72d3e35","name":"Nielsen, Cecilie Heide","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","first":"Marianne","key":"thomsenmariannepau","last":"Thomsen","locid":"a829b47d-f5d2-404d-b768-ec12fbb3b661","name":"Thomsen, Marianne","orcid":"0000-0003-2453-5141","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.2926/208135","isbn":["9789294050113"],"pages":"210","publisher":"Publication Office of the European Union","status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-6d8f8981-e507-4df8-baa5-8c71451deab1","ku-ebbef884-e2e6-4d13-87b2-cb4586283a4b"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Algae and Climate : Final Report","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-097.44-704163","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Introduction: In Denmark, multiple national initiatives have been associated with improved bystander defibrillation and survival following out-of-hospital cardiac arrest (OHCA) in public places. However, OHCAs in residential neighbourhoods continue to have poor outcomes. The Cardiac Arrest in Residential Areas with MoBile volunteer responder Activation trial aims to improve bystander defibrillation and survival following OHCA in residential neighbourhoods with a high risk of OHCA. The intervention consists of: (1) strategically deployed automated external defibrillators accessible at all hours, (2) cardiopulmonary resuscitation (CPR) training of residents and (3) recruitment of residents for a volunteer responder programme. Methods and analysis: This is a prospective, pair-matched, cluster-randomised, superiority trial with clusters of 26 residential neighbourhoods, testing the effectiveness of the intervention in a real-world setting. The areas are randomised for intervention or control. Intervention and control areas will receive the standard OHCA emergency response, including volunteer responder activation. However, targeted automated external defibrillator deployment, CPR training and volunteer responder recruitment will only be provided in the intervention areas. The primary outcome is bystander defibrillation, and the secondary outcome is 30-day survival. Data on patients who had an OHCA will be collected through the Danish Cardiac Arrest Registry. Ethics and dissemination: Approval to store OHCA data has been granted from the Legal Office, Capital Region of Denmark (j.nr: 2012-58-0004, VD-2018-28, I-Suite no: 6222, and P-2021-670). In Denmark, formal approval from the ethics committee is only obtainable when the study regards testing medicine or medical equipment on humans or using genome or diagnostic imagine as data source. The Ethics Committee of the Capital Region of Denmark has evaluated the trial and waived formal approval unnecessary (H-19037170). Results will be published in peer-reviewed papers and shared with funders, stakeholders, and housing organisations through summaries and presentations. Trial registration number: ClinicalTrials.gov Registry (NCT04446585).","author_count":12,"contributors":["Juul Grabmayr, Anne","Malta Hansen, Carolina","Bo, Nanna","Sheikh, Annam Pervez","Hassager, Christian","Ersbøll, Annette Kjær","Kjaergaard, Jesper","Lippert, Freddy","Tjørnhøj-Thomsen, Tine","Gislason, Gunnar","Torp-Pedersen, Christian","Folke, Fredrik"],"cuid":["S02-099.95-716402"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Juul Grabmayr, Anne"],"keyword":["Adult cardiology","Cardiology","Cardiopulmonary resuscitation","Clinical trial","Defibrillators","Out of hospital cardiac arrest"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"OT":["National Institute of Public Health"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"community intervention to improve defibrillation before ambulance arrival in residential neighbourhoods with a high risk of out of hospital cardiac arrest study protocol of a cluster randomised trial the caramba trial","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1136/bmjopen-2023-073541","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-099.95-716402","identifier":[{"id":"85175450456","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC10565309","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"37816557","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-55ec162e-b9b4-4fb1-a8eb-2e932764e3c3","sdu-653f2c67-ca0a-4553-b187-4504433fb69f"],"keyword":["Adult cardiology","CARDIOLOGY","Cardiopulmonary Resuscitation","Clinical Trial","Defibrillators","Out-of-Hospital Cardiac Arrest"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-A90B642C6F04C21EAF76F5CFBBF543B9"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1136/bmjopen-2023-073541","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/375729242/e073541.full.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/245581584/e073541.full.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, National Institute of Public Health","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, National Institute of Public Health, Geographical and registerbased epidemiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl"