{"abstract":"Dyrkning, høst og anvendelse af tang kan være ét af mange nødvendige virkemidler, vi skal bruge for at dreje verden i en mere bæredygtig retning. Du får her en aktuel status på mulighederne og udfordringerne i at anvende tang til for eksempel bæredygtige fødevarer og dyrefoder.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Bruhn, Annette","Mouritsen, Lone Thybo","Holdt, Susan","Thomsen, Marianne","Weisbjerg, Martin Riis"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-029353"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Bruhn, Annette","Holdt, Susan Løvstad","Mouritsen, Lone Thybo","Thomsen, Marianne","Weisbjerg, Martin Riis"],"level":"pop","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Kattegatcentret"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"tang kan bidrage til grønne løsninger","src":["au","dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/270212772/AN1_2022_tang.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-029353","ids":["au-e624b77d-be06-41d4-8ad4-90813e4f924c","dtu-4194fa1c-f300-4e51-9aa5-7073f7e6fd16"],"lang":"English","level":"Popular","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-2-22DDE86E525D957D9FEB67067C67F610"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://aktuelnaturvidenskab.dk/find-artikel/nyeste-numre/1-2022/tang-kan-bidrage-til-groenne-loesninger","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/235114727/AN1_2022_tang.pdf","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/270212772/AN1_2022_tang.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, CBIO - Centre for Circular Bioeconomy, Foulum, CBIO - Centre for Circular Bioeconomy, Foulum - CBIO - Centre for Circular Bioeconomy, Bartholins Allé","Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Ecoscience, Department of Ecoscience - Marine Ecology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Kattegatcentret"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Food Institute","Technical University of Denmark, National Food Institute, Research Group for Bioactives – Analysis and Application"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Annette","key":"bruhnpau","last":"Bruhn","locid":"15559017-3036-4e04-968e-338a24d800ce","name":"Bruhn, Annette","orcid":"0000-0002-7940-1338","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lone Thybo","key":"mouritsenpau","last":"Mouritsen","name":"Mouritsen, Lone Thybo","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Susan","key":"holdtpau","last":"Holdt","locid":"14f42614-f9fe-47a7-a5c7-a7a0d7df7db9","name":"Holdt, Susan Løvstad","name_org":"Holdt, Susan","orcid":"0000-0002-6888-782X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Marianne","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","name":"Thomsen, Marianne","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Martin Riis","key":"weisbjergpau","last":"Weisbjerg","locid":"501c877c-de2b-4cd2-9f3c-42e223238a40","name":"Weisbjerg, Martin Riis","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["13992309"],"issue":"1","journal":"Aktuel Naturvidenskab","pages":"8-12","status":"p","title":"Aktuel Naturvidenskab","volume":"1-2022"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-e624b77d-be06-41d4-8ad4-90813e4f924c","dtu-4194fa1c-f300-4e51-9aa5-7073f7e6fd16"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Tang kan bidrage til grønne løsninger","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-029353","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Background: Inguinal lymph node dissection (ILND) is associated with a high complication rate. Retrospective studies suggest that incisional negative pressure wound therapy (iNPWT) might reduce complications, especially seroma, following ILND. Methods: This was a prospective multicenter, randomized (1:1), open-labeled, parallel-group trial. Patients with macrometastic melanoma to the inguinal lymph nodes and eligible for ILND were randomized to receive either iNPWT for 14 postoperative days or conventional wound dressing. The primary outcome was seroma incidence. Secondary outcomes included surgical-site infection, wound rupture, wound necrosis, hematoma, rehospitalization and readmission rates between groups. All outcomes were registered 3 months after ILND and analyzed according to the intention-to-treat principle. Results: The trial was terminated early due to a low recruitment rate as a consequence of a change in the national treatment protocol, and the estimated sample size was not reached. Twenty patients were included and randomized in the study. The trial showed less seroma formation between the iNPWT 6/11 (55%) and control 7/9 (78%) groups; however, this was not statistically significant (p = 0.29). Similarly, there were no differences in the rates of surgical-site infection (p = 0.63), wound rupture (p = 0.19), wound necrosis (p = 0.82), hematoma (p = 0.19), reoperation (p = 0.82) or readmission (p = 0.34) between groups. Conclusion: There was a tendency toward fewer complications in the iNPWT group, however this trial was underpowered and could not confirm the hypothesis that iNPWT reduces complications after ILND. Future randomized controlled trials are required to fully evaluate the treatment potential of iNPWT. Trial registration: The trial was prospectively registered at https://clinicaltrials.gov/ct2/show/NCT03433937.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Jørgensen, Mads Gustaf","Chakera, Annette Hougaard","Hölmich, Lisbet Rosenkrantz","Drejøe, Jennifer Berg","Andersen, Pia Cajsa Leth","Khorasani, Hoda","Toyserkani, Navid Mohamadpour","Thomsen, Jørn Bo","Sørensen, Jens Ahm"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-041539"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Jørgensen, Mads Gustaf"],"keyword":["Complications","Lymph node dissection","Melanoma","Negative Pressure Wound Therapy","PICO","Seroma","VAC"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"can prophylactic incisional negative pressure wound therapy reduce wound complications after inguinal lymph node dissection for melanoma results from a randomized controlled trial","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jpra.2022.08.003","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The company Smith&Nephew granted the iNPWT devices used in this study to JAS (grant number IIS 486). The grant was unrestricted. The grant provider did not have influence on the study design, data collection, data analysis, decision to terminate the trial earlier than anticipated, interpretation of results, or report writing."],"id":"S02-100.00-041539","identifier":[{"id":"PMC9593268","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85141865119","type":"scopus"},{"id":"36304071","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-389f9ae9-8058-4c4e-8191-4b0596e4bed3","sdu-69d7f741-3c8d-4404-9def-91efc3c51f85"],"keyword":["Complications","Lymph node dissection","Melanoma","Negative-pressure wound therapy","PICO","Seroma","VAC"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-00E1E15CB29DD82AD9B3E91268536B70"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jpra.2022.08.003","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/340535896/1_s2.0_S2352587822000614_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/214323496/1_s2.0_S2352587822000614_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research Unit OPEN (Odense)","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Plastic Surgery (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"region of southern denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-SDR","l3nl":"Region of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"Region of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region of Southern Denmark","namevar":["Odense University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-SDR","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Plastic Surgery"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"dk","key":"region zealand","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-ZEA","l3nl":"Region Zealand","l3nn":"Region Zealand","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region Zealand","namevar":["Zealand University Hospital, Roskilde"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-ZEA","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Mads Gustaf","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"aebe7465-c8a9-452a-9b45-6259e674c2ee","name":"Jørgensen, Mads Gustaf","orcid":"0000-0002-8755-3446","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Annette Hougaard","key":"chakerapau","last":"Chakera","locid":"4464560d-a9f0-425c-9c26-441b1b6c26a1","name":"Chakera, Annette H.","name_org":"Chakera, Annette Hougaard","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Lisbet Rosenkrantz","key":"hölmichpau","last":"Hölmich","locid":"762c4ddb-9f7d-4dad-a26f-5546c897eda0","name":"Hölmich, Lisbet Rosenkrantz","orcid":"0000-0002-1983-5222","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Jennifer Berg","key":"drejøepau","last":"Drejøe","name":"Drejøe, Jennifer Berg","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Pia Cajsa Leth","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Pia Cajsa Leth","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Hoda","key":"khorasanipau","last":"Khorasani","name":"Khorasani, Hoda","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 5","corresponding":null,"first":"Navid Mohamadpour","key":"toyserkanipau","last":"Toyserkani","name":"Toyserkani, Navid Mohamadpour","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jørn Bo","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","locid":"b2cefe25-2acb-4fd9-971a-2bf4c209b85e","name":"Thomsen, Jørn Bo","orcid":"0000-0002-7368-6133","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens Ahm","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"267cd59a-3918-47db-8d23-54015d770b6c","name":"Sørensen, Jens Ahm","orcid":"0000-0003-4903-0094","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36304071"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jpra.2022.08.003","issn":["23525878"],"journal":"JPRAS Open","pages":"134-143","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"JPRAS Open","volume":"34"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85141865119"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-389f9ae9-8058-4c4e-8191-4b0596e4bed3","sdu-69d7f741-3c8d-4404-9def-91efc3c51f85"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Can prophylactic incisional negative pressure wound therapy Reduce Wound Complications After Inguinal Lymph Node Dissection for Melanoma? Results from a Randomized Controlled Trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-041539","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Brain homeostasis depends on the existence of the blood-brain barrier (BBB). Despite decades of research, the factors and signalling pathways for modulating and maintaining BBB integrity are not fully elucidated. Here, we characterize the expression and function of the multifunctional receptor, sortilin, in the cells of the BBB, in vivo and in vitro. We show that sortilin acts as an important regulatory protein of the BBB's tightness. In rats lacking sortilin, the BBB was leaky, which correlated well with relocated distribution of the localisation of zonula occludens-1, VE-cadherin and β-catenin junctional proteins. Furthermore, the absence of sortilin in brain endothelial cells resulted in decreased phosphorylation of Akt signalling protein and increased the level of phospho-ERK1/2. As a putative result of MAPK/ERK pathways activity, the junctions between the brain endothelial cells were disintegrated and the integrity of the BBB became compromised. The identified barrier differences between wild type and Sort1-/- brain endothelial cells can pave the way for a better understanding of sortilin's role in the healthy and diseased BBB.","author_count":16,"contributors":["Toth, Andrea E","Helms, Hans C","Harazin, Andras","Johnsen, Kasper B","Goldeman, Charlotte","Burkhart, Annette","Thomsen, Maj Schneider","Kempen, Paul J","Klepe, Adrian","Lipka, Dora V","Møller, Peter L","Andresen, Thomas L","Nyegaard, Mette","Moos, Torben","Brodin, Birger","Nielsen, Morten S"],"cuid":["S04-091.98-011856"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"corresponding_author":["Nielsen, Morten S","Nielsen, Morten Schallburg"],"keyword":["Adherent junction","Animals","Blood Brain Barrier metabolism","Blood brain barrier","Brain endothelial cells","Cells Cultured","Rats","Rats Sprague Dawley","Sortilin","Tight junction"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci","soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-LUND"],"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-NP-LUND","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"sortilin regulates blood brain barrier integrity","src":["aau","au","dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/febs.16225","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S04-091.98-011856","identifier":[{"id":"000709002100001","type":"wos"},{"id":"85117310529","type":"scopus"},{"id":"34626084","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-f84119c8-0b9b-4c47-bebe-1d6e0a24d2cd","au-132eb428-1186-40eb-9025-ab1a106b5cbc","dtu-07d3d318-215b-4b4d-8917-12b78846ad53","ku-07847459-e4b3-44ac-a2aa-5b2dd4cfee1e"],"keyword":["Adaptor Proteins, Vesicular Transport/deficiency","Animals","Blood-Brain Barrier/metabolism","Cells, Cultured","Rats","Rats, Sprague-Dawley","adherent junction","blood–brain barrier","brain endothelial cells","sortilin","tight junction"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology","Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-7-5AA8BE6BDD0127A64C34F08E72AF288A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/359088581/489514921_2_39.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/449995390/febs.16225.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/febs.16225","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/258366510/pesei_febs.16225.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities",