694","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34626084"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/febs.16225","issn":["14321033","1742464X"],"issn_org":["17424658"],"issue":"4","journal":"FEBS Journal","pages":"1062-1079","publisher":"Wiley-Blackwell Publishing Ltd","publisher_org":"Wiley-Blackwell Publishing Ltd.","status":"p","title":"FEBS Journal","title_org":"FEBS journal","volume":"289"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85117310529"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Non-Profit Organisations","Other Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-f84119c8-0b9b-4c47-bebe-1d6e0a24d2cd","au-132eb428-1186-40eb-9025-ab1a106b5cbc","dtu-07d3d318-215b-4b4d-8917-12b78846ad53","ku-07847459-e4b3-44ac-a2aa-5b2dd4cfee1e"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Sortilin regulates blood-brain barrier integrity","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S04-091.98-011856","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Overexpression of α-synuclein with tyrosine mutated to phenylalanine at position 125 leads to a severe phenotype with motor impairment and neuropathology in Drosophila. Here, we hypothesized that tyrosine mutations would similarly lead to impaired motor performance with neuropathology in a rodent model. In transgenic mice (ASO), tyrosines at positions 125, 133, and 136 in human α-synuclein were mutated to phenylalanine and cloned into a Thy1.2 expression vector, which was used to create transgenic mouse lines on a mixed genetic background TgN(Thy-1-SNCA-YF)4Emfu (YF). The YF mice had a decreased lifespan and displayed a dramatic motor phenotype with paralysis of both hind- and forelegs. Post-translational modification of α-synuclein due to phosphorylation of serine 129 is often seen in inclusions in the brains of patients with α-synucleinopathies. We observed a slight but significant increase in phosphorylation of serine 129 in the cytosol in YF mice compared to age-matched human α-synuclein transgenic mice (ASO). Conversely, significantly decreased phosphorylation of serine 129 was seen in synaptosomes of YF mice that also contained higher amounts of soluble oligomers. YF mice deposited full-length α-synuclein aggregates in neurons widespread in the CNS with the main occurrence in the forebrain structures of the cerebral cortex, the basal ganglia, and limbic structures. Full-length α-synuclein labeling was also prominent in many nuclear regions of the brain stem, deep cerebellar nuclei, and cerebellar cortex. The study shows that the substitution of tyrosines to phenylalanine in α-synuclein at positions 125, 133, and 136 leads to severe toxicity in vivo. An insignificant change upon tyrosine substitution suggests that the phosphorylation of serine 129 is not the cause of the toxicity.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Lassen, Louise Berkhoudt","Thomsen, Maj Schneider","Basso, Elisa","Füchtbauer, Ernst-Martin","Füchtbauer, Annette","Outeiro, Tiago Fleming","Jensen, Poul Henning","Moos, Torben"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-011631"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Moos, Torben"],"country":["Germany","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Max Planck Institute for Biophysical Chemistry (Karl Friedrich Bonhoeffer Institute)","Max Planck Institute for Multidisciplinary Sciences","Newcastle University","University Medical Center Göttingen","University of Göttingen"],"keyword":["Aggregates","Alpha synuclein","Animals","Behavior","Humans","Mice","Mice Transgenic","Mutation genetics","Neurodegeneration","Neurotoxicity Syndromes","Oligodendrocyte","Parkinson s disease","Phenylalanine","Serine","Serine genetics","Transgene","Tyrosine","alpha Synuclein genetics","cortico spinal tract"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"mutation of tyrosine sites in the human alpha synuclein gene induces neurotoxicity in transgenic mice with soluble alpha synuclein oligomer formation","src":["aau","au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/cells11223673","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-011631","identifier":[{"id":"PMC9688722","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"36429099","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85142454431","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-f37ef3f1-1e09-4f6e-a998-d782e0c6c50e","au-4343cfbb-bc73-4418-9482-866aa6e4cecd"],"keyword":["Animals","Humans","Mice","Mice, Transgenic","Mutation/genetics","Neurotoxicity Syndromes","Parkinson’s disease","Phenylalanine","Serine/genetics","aggregates","alpha-Synuclein/genetics","alpha-synuclein","behavior","cortico-spinal tract","neurodegeneration","oligodendrocyte","serine","transgene","tyrosine"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-F6260D76BC186F48EEEFD3E73D65CFC1"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/502931430/cells_11_03673_v2.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/cells11223673","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Biomedicine, Department of Biomedicine - Forskning og uddannelse, Vest","Aarhus University, Interfaculty Centre, DANDRITE, DANDRITE - Jensen Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, Neurobiology Research and Drug Delivery"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"university medical center göttingen","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University Medical Center Göttingen","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"de","key":"university of göttingen","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Göttingen","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"de","key":"max planck institute for biophysical chemistry","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU"