.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael","key":"skaaruppau","last":"Skaarup","name":"Skaarup, Michael","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Niels","key":"kleisfrederiksenpau","last":"Kleis Frederiksen","name":"Kleis Frederiksen, Niels","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Camilla","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","name":"Christensen, Camilla","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Hauskov","key":"pilgaardpau","last":"Pilgaard","name":"Pilgaard, Søren Hauskov","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Hasan","key":"dönmezpau","last":"Dönmez","name":"Dönmez, Hasan","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Annette","key":"norupthomsenpau","last":"Norup Thomsen","name":"Norup Thomsen, Annette","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"65","place":"København","publisher":"Skatteministeriet","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Non-Profit Organisations","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["cbs-02f6de58-1465-4984-b73b-9e0625dd6cce"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School"],"title":"Beskatning ved overdragelse af erhvervsvirksomheder til erhvervsdrivende fonde : Rapport fra Arbejdsgruppen om Succession til Erhvervsdrivende Fonde","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-275701","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Introduction Socially vulnerable and homeless peoples’ life situation is characterized by combined social, physical and mental problems resulting in complex health care needs. Yet, they are hard to reach and often do not seek or want help. Consequently, their life expectancy is found to be remarkably lower than for the general populations. In Denmark, the first mobile clinic “the Sociolance” has been operating as a pilot project in the period from December 2015 to August 2017 (with a subsequently extension of the service). The aim of the Sociolance is to assist socially vulnerable and homeless people in the capital city of Denmark, Copenhagen, with social and healthcare problems not requiring an emergency ambulance. The Sociolance is unique at an international level since it combines affiliation with the Emergency Medical Dispatch center, from where it is requested, with performing social outreach work. The Sociolance renders help on the spot and transports users to relevant offers. The aim of this study is twofold: 1) to describe the trips of the Sociolance and 2) to characterize the people using the services of the Sociolance, including describing to what extent the users of the Sociolance accept referrals to social and healthcare services offered by the staff of the Sociolance. Methods Data used for this study were collected in the study period between December 2015 and June 2017 from several sources: 1) electronically registered data from the emergency medical service database, 2) record sheets completed by the social workers in contact with the users of the Sociolance, and 3) case reports fulfilled by the staff (social worker and paramedic) daily at the end of each shift. We performed descriptive analyses using frequency distribution indicating the number of observations and percentages, and the mean and interquartile range. Results In total, 2,072 transportations were registered in the study period. Of all transportations, 83% were related to requested transportations through the Emergency Medical Dispatch center. A requested transportation took in average 62 minutes (38-80 minutes) including 27 minutes spent with the user at the destination and 15 minutes spent with the user at the hospital. A total of 917 users (77% male) were registered in the study period with over half (58%) of the contacts registered in the street environment. Every third user in contact with the service was affected by alcohol or influenced by drug and around one out of four (26%) were mentally affected. One third were registered as homeless and nearly one out of five (18.6%) users was registered with another ethnicity than Danish. Approximately 40% of the users were connected to the social service system. Nine out of ten users were offered social – and/or healthcare services in contact with the Sociolance and three out of four accepted the offer they received. The users were referred to health care services related to substance abuse (40%), mental illness (20%) and somatic disease (13%), respectively. Nearly one out of four users were offered services related to combined healthcare (substance abuse and/or mental disease and/or somatic illness). Of social care, one out of five users were transported to housing services/shelters. Conclusions The majority of the Sociolance transportations were made by request through the Emergency Medical Dispatch center unleashing resources for the use of emergency ambulances. The population in contact with the Sociolance had often severe combined health and social problems. It was found that, the acceptance of the services offered by the Sociolance was quite high demonstrating it to be an important approach in the effort to target “hard to reach” populations.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Kristensen, Marie Skov","Ahlmark, Nanna","Tjørnhøj-Thomsen, Tine","Ersbøll, Annette Kjær"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-590683"],"event":{"end":"2018-07-06","place":"Lyon, fr","start":"2018-07-04","title":"European Congress of Epidemiology","year":"2018"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the sociolance a mobile clinic requested through emergency medical dispatch center serving socially vulnerable and homeless people in the capital city of denmark","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-590683","ids":["sdu-3cd92dbd-d903-475f-acd8-d8f0d12c0bd0"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-F61247F812BCACFFE671A33E2B801CC1"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, National Institute of Public Health, Department of Population Health and Morbidity"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marie Skov","key":"kristensenpau","last":"Kristensen","locid":"ede804e9-f7b6-414e-a9bd-557cb33be5bb","name":"Kristensen, Marie Skov","orcid":"0000-0002-8066-8937","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nanna","key":"ahlmarkpau","last":"Ahlmark","locid":"e0827fca-2d67-4509-a999-d67446ccb462","name":"Ahlmark, Nanna","orcid":"0000-0002-0539-2061","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Tine","key":"tjørnhøjthomsenpau","last":"Tjørnhøj-Thomsen","locid":"bc043d50-4a2b-41c1-a085-da4a674866f3","name":"Tjørnhøj-Thomsen, Tine","orcid":"0000-0003-3621-6682","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Annette Kjær","key":"ersbøllpau","last":"Ersbøll","locid":"ba343517-a6c5-47c1-a8ba-4cbe00b7409c","name":"Ersbøll, Annette Kjær","orcid":"0000-0002-9407-3387","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-3cd92dbd-d903-475f-acd8-d8f0d12c0bd0"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"The Sociolance: a mobile clinic requested through Emergency Medical Dispatch center serving socially vulnerable and homeless people in the capital city of Denmark","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-590683","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Genome-wide association studies (GWAS) have transformed our understanding of susceptibility to multiple myeloma (MM), but much of the heritability remains unexplained. We report a new GWAS, a meta-analysis with previous GWAS and a replication series, totalling 9974 MM cases and 247,556 controls of European ancestry. Collectively, these data provide evidence for six new MM risk loci, bringing the total number to 23. Integration of information from gene expression, epigenetic profiling and in situ Hi-C data for the 23 risk loci implicate disruption of developmental transcriptional regulators as a basis of MM susceptibility, compatible with altered B-cell differentiation as a key mechanism. Dysregulation of autophagy/apoptosis and cell cycle signalling feature as recurrently perturbed pathways. Our findings provide further insight into the biological basis of MM.","author_count":53,"contributors":["Went, Molly","Sud, Amit","Försti, Asta","Halvarsson, Britt-Marie","Weinhold, Niels","Kimber, Scott","van Duin, Mark","Thorleifsson, Gudmar","Holroyd, Amy","Johnson, David C","Li, Ni","Orlando, Giulia","Law, Philip J","Ali, Mina","Chen, Bowang","Mitchell, Jonathan S","Gudbjartsson, Daniel F","Kuiper, Rowan","Stephens, Owen W","Bertsch, Uta","Broderick, Peter","Campo, Chiara","Bandapalli, Obul R","Einsele, Hermann","Gregory, Walter A","Gullberg, Urban","Hillengass, Jens","Hoffmann, Per","Jackson, Graham H","Jöckel, Karl-Heinz","Johnsson, Ellinor","Kristinsson, Sigurður Y","Mellqvist, Ulf-Henrik","Nahi, Hareth","Easton, Douglas","Pharoah, Paul","Dunning, Alison","Peto, Julian","Canzian, Federico","Swerdlow, Anthony","Eeles, Rosalind A","Kote-Jarai, ZSofia","Muir, Kenneth","Pashayan, Nora","Nickel, Jolanta","Nöthen, Markus M","Rafnar, Thorunn","Thomsen, Hauke","Andersen, Niels Frost","Sørensen, Karina Dalsgaard"],"cuid":["S02-098.44-029570"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"51-200 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corpau":["The PRACTICAL Consortium"],"country":["Germany","Iceland","Netherlands","Sweden","Switzerland","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Center for Hematology and Regenerative Medicine","Division of Genetics and Epidemiology","Erasmus University Medical Centre","Erasmus University Rotterdam","German Cancer Research Center","German Cancer Research Center (DKFZ)","Harvard University","Heidelberg University ","Hematology and Transfusion Medicine","Institute of Cancer Research","Landspitali University Hospital","London School of Hygiene and Tropical Medicine","Lund University","National Centre of Tumor Diseases","Newcastle University","Royal Marsden Hospital London","Royal Marsden NHS Foundation Trust","Royal Victoria Infirmary","University College London","University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences","University of Basel","University of Bonn","University of Cambridge","University of Duisburg-Essen","University of Gothenburg","University of Iceland","University of Leeds","University of Manchester","University of Warwick","University of Würzburg","deCODE Genetics"],"keyword":["Ankyrin Repeat","Architecture","Bayes Theorem","CELLS","Chromatin Immunoprecipitation","Chromatin chemistry","Complex","European Continental Ancestry Group genetics","Female","Gene Expression Regulation","Gene expression","Genetic Predisposition to Disease","Genome Wide Association Study","Genotype","Heritability","Humans","Male","Multiple Myeloma genetics","Polymorphism","Polymorphism Single Nucleotide","Promoter Regions Genetic","Quality control","Quantitative Trait Loci","Risk"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"identification of multiple risk loci and regulatory mechanisms influencing susceptibility to multiple myeloma incl author correction","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-018-04989-w","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-098.44-029570","identifier":[{"id":"000444493600001","type":"wos"},{"id":"PMC6137048","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85053336514","type":"scopus"},{"id":"30213928","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-e9249fc9-95ae-4bb0-abf9-491eb11b5c2e","ku-bcfc7cac-f928-415e-8b03-ff9ac2c62d5e"],"keyword":["ANKYRIN REPEAT","ARCHITECTURE","Bayes Theorem","CASE-CONTROL ASSOCIATION","CELLS","COMPLEX","Chromatin Immunoprecipitation","Chromatin/chemistry","European Continental Ancestry Group/genetics","Female","GENE-EXPRESSION","Gene Expression Regulation","Genetic Predisposition to Disease","Genome-Wide Association Study","Genotype","HERITABILITY","Humans","Male","Multiple Myeloma/genetics","POLYMORPHISM","Polymorphism, Single Nucleotide","Promoter Regions, Genetic","Quality Control","Quantitative Trait Loci","Risk","SOCS BOX","TACI"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-F4B23E3C8DF0C45CF58C9AE4DA110797"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/209545168/s41467_018_04989_w.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-018-04989-w","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"gb","key":"institute of cancer research","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Institute of Cancer Research","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"lund university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Lund University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"german cancer resear