6514"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-e9249fc9-95ae-4bb0-abf9-491eb11b5c2e","ku-bcfc7cac-f928-415e-8b03-ff9ac2c62d5e"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Identification of multiple risk loci and regulatory mechanisms influencing susceptibility to multiple myeloma : [incl. author correction]","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-098.44-029570","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Rationale: The ability to treat invalidating neurological diseases is impeded by the presence of the blood-brain barrier (BBB), which inhibits the transport of most blood-borne substances into the brain parenchyma. Targeting the transferrin receptor (TfR) on the surface of brain capillaries has been a popular strategy to give a preferential accumulation of drugs or nanomedicines, but several aspects of this targeting strategy remain elusive. Here we report that TfR-targeted gold nanoparticles (AuNPs) can accumulate in brain capillaries and further transport across the BBB to enter the brain parenchyma. Methods: We characterized our targeting strategy both in vitro using primary models of the BBB and in vivo using quantitative measurements of gold accumulation by inductively-coupled plasma-mass spectrometry together with morphological assessments using light microscopy after silver enhancement and transmission electron microscopy with energy-dispersive X-ray spectroscopy. Results: We find that the uptake capacity is significantly modulated by the affinity and valency of the AuNP-conjugated antibodies. Specifically, antibodies with high and low affinities mediate a low and intermediate uptake of AuNPs into the brain, respectively, whereas a monovalent (bi-specific) antibody improves the uptake capacity remarkably. Conclusion: Our findings indicate that monovalent ligands may be beneficial for obtaining transcytosis of TfR-targeted nanomedicines across the BBB, which is relevant for future design of nanomedicines for brain drug delivery.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Johnsen, Kasper Bendix","Bak, Martin","Kempen, Paul Joseph","Melander, Fredrik","Burkhart, Annette","Thomsen, Maj Schneider","Nielsen, Morten Schallburg","Moos, Torben","Andresen, Thomas Lars"],"cuid":["S03-099.96-006648"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corresponding_author":["Andresen, Thomas Lars"],"keyword":["Affinity","Brain drug delivery","Gold nanoparticle","Targeting","Transferrin receptor"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"antibody affinity and valency impact brain uptake of transferrin receptor targeted gold nanoparticles","src":["aau","au","dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.7150/thno.25228","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-099.96-006648","identifier":[{"id":"29930740","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC6010987","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85047512631","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-89564bc0-de0f-45d6-8801-1770f748a793","au-8661074c-cbd5-4084-95fa-e16f2c1cba9c","dtu-6a77c4be-06c3-47bb-83df-03b4e78e7172"],"keyword":["Affinity","Brain drug delivery","Gold nanoparticle","Targeting","Transferrin receptor"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-285326655E9F0A7660A4EF4AB5B24E38"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/150422190/thnov08p3416.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.7150/thno.25228","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/283286848/v08p3416.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aa