{"abstract":"En gruppe mænd i alderen 45-65 år i Aalborg Kommune er blevet identificeret med risikabel sundhedsadfærd ift. alkoholforbrug, rygning og fysisk aktivitetsniveau. Mændene har manglende eller sparsom kontakt til sundheds- og/eller socialområdet, og gør tilsyneladende ikke brug af tilgængelige kommunale sundheds tilbud. Dette medvirker til øget ulighed i sundhed for denne gruppe borgere. Det overordnede formål med ph.d. projektet er at frembringe viden, der kan bruges som baggrund for tidlig opsporing af sundhedsudfordringer hos målgruppen.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Pedersen, Annette","Haslund-Thomsen, Helle Lønstrup","Curtis, Tine","Grønkjær, Mette"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-009270"],"event":{"end":"2017-08-25","place":"Aalborg, dk","start":"2017-08-22","title":"Nordisk Folkesundhedskonference","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Sundhed ernæring og livskvalitet"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-NDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"],"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-UCN"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-NDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-UC-UCN"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"tidlig opsporing af sundhedsudfordringer hos midaldrende mænd i aalborg kommune","src":["aau","ucn"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-UC-UCN"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.nordiskfolkesundhedskonference.dk/media/1241/23-pedersen-haslund-curtis-groenkjaer.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-009270","ids":["aau-c036e211-7ac6-40d1-91d9-037049de56fc","ucn-e695c6ef-eeee-4f16-908e-b1bd85c82231"],"keyword":["Sundhed, ernæring og livskvalitet"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-2-083A8F842FFC9F2DF3C5D70967D77339"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.nordiskfolkesundhedskonference.dk/media/1241/23-pedersen-haslund-curtis-groenkjaer.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://nordiskfolkesundhedskonference.dk/media/1241/23-pedersen-haslund-curtis-groenkjaer.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ucn university college of northern denmark","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-UCN","l3nl":"University College of Northern Denmark","l3nn":"UCN University College of Northern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"UCN University College of Northern Denmark","namevar":["Professionshøjskolen UCN, UCN Direktion, UCN Velfærd, Sygeplejerskeuddannelsen Aalborg"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-UCN","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"north denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-NDR","l3nl":"North Denmark Region","l3nn":"North Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"North Denmark Region","namevar":["Aalborg Universitetshospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-NDR","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Annette","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"20e7ece3-a0ad-4f51-b8f8-c4ff1989a272","name":"Pedersen, Annette","orcid":"0000-0002-7267-2856","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Helle","key":"haslundpau","last":"Haslund","locid":"7c65e556-5085-4d87-b1f3-e611d15eb594","name":"Haslund-Thomsen, Helle Lønstrup","name_org":"Haslund, Helle","orcid":"0000-0002-5260-9155","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tine","key":"curtispau","last":"Curtis","locid":"360a65e7-1be8-4fb5-a513-6d21a834ba50","name":"Curtis, Tine","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mette","key":"grønkjærpau","last":"Grønkjær","locid":"574b63eb-8aff-43ac-b907-12a665ace204","name":"Grønkjær, Mette","orcid":"0000-0003-1558-7062","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Universities","University College of Northern Denmark","University Colleges"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-c036e211-7ac6-40d1-91d9-037049de56fc","ucn-e695c6ef-eeee-4f16-908e-b1bd85c82231"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","UCN University College of Northern Denmark"],"title":"Tidlig opsporing af sundhedsudfordringer hos midaldrende mænd i Aalborg Kommune","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-009270","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: School cardiopulmonary resuscitation (CPR) training has become mandatory in many countries, but whether legislation has translated into implementation of CPR training is largely unknown. We assessed CPR training of students following 8 years of legislative mandates in Denmark. METHODS AND RESULTS: A nationwide cross-sectional survey of Danish school leadership (n=1240) and ninth-grade homeroom teachers (n=1381) was carried out for school year 2013-2014. Qualitative interviews and the Theory of Planned Behavior were used to construct the survey. Logistic regression models were employed to identify factors associated with completed CPR training. Information from 63.1% of eligible schools was collected: 49.3% (n=611) of leadership and 48.2% (n=665) of teachers responded. According to teachers, 28.4% (95% CI 25.0% to 32.0%) and 10.3% (95% CI 8.1% to 12.8%) of eligible classes had completed CPR and automated external defibrillator training, respectively. Among leadership, 60.2% (95% CI 56.2% to 64.1%) reported CPR training had occurred during the 3 years prior to the survey. Factors associated with completed CPR training included believing other schools were conducting training (odds ratio [OR] 9.68 [95% CI 4.65-20.1]), awareness of mandating legislation (OR 4.19 [95% CI 2.65-6.62]), presence of a school CPR training coordinator (OR 3.01 [95% CI 1.84-4.92]), teacher feeling competent to conduct training (OR 2.78 [95% CI 1.74-4.45]), and having easy access to training material (OR 2.08 [95% CI 1.57-2.76]). CONCLUSIONS: Despite mandating legislation, school CPR training has not been successfully implemented. Completed CPR training was associated with believing other schools were conducting training, awareness of mandating legislation, presence of a school CPR training coordinator, teachers teacher feeling competent to conduct training, and having easy access to training material. Facilitating these factors may increase rates of school CPR training.