{"abstract":"The mechanisms for iron transport through the blood-brain barrier (BBB) remain a controversy. We analyzed for expression of mRNA and proteins involved in oxidation and transport of iron in isolated brain capillaries from dietary normal, iron-deficient, and iron-reverted rats. The expression was also investigated in isolated rat brain endothelial cells (RBECs) and in immortalized rat brain endothelial (RBE4) cells grown as monoculture or in hanging culture inserts with defined BBB properties. Transferrin receptor 1, ferrireductases Steap 2 and 3, divalent metal transporter 1 (DMT1), ferroportin, soluble and glycosylphosphatidylinositol (GPI)-anchored ceruloplasmin, and hephaestin were all expressed in brain capillaries in vivo and in isolated RBECs and RBE4 cells. Gene expression of DMT1, ferroportin, and soluble and GPI-anchored ceruloplasmin were significantly higher in isolated RBECs with induced BBB properties. Primary pericytes and astrocytes both expressed ceruloplasmin and hephaestin, and RBECs, pericytes, and astrocytes all exhibited ferrous oxidase activity. The coherent protein expression of these genes was demonstrated by immunocytochemistry. The data show that brain endothelial cells provide the machinery for receptor-mediated uptake of ferric iron-containing transferrin. Ferric iron can then undergo reduction to ferrous iron by ferrireductases inside endosomes followed by DMT1-mediated pumping into the cytosol and subsequently cellular export by ferroportin. The expression of soluble ceruloplasmin by brain endothelial cells, pericytes, and astrocytes that together form the neurovascular unit (NVU) provides the ferroxidase activity necessary to reoxidize ferrous iron once released inside the brain.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Burkhart, Annette","Skjørringe, Tina","Johnsen, Kasper Bendix","Siupka, Piotr","Thomsen, Louiza Bohn","Nielsen, Morten Schallburg","Thomsen, Lars Lykke","Moos, Torben"],"cuid":["S02-095.56-003425"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"expression of iron related proteins at the neurovascular unit supports reduction and reoxidation of iron for transport through the blood brain barrier","src":["aau","au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84994754057","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-095.56-003425","identifier":[{"id":"WOS:000387870200056","type":"wos"},{"id":"84994754057","type":"scopus"},{"id":"26687231","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-45f6c2cf-db97-42af-84f2-97d3ff6a2b88","au-d9686599-1e70-4a75-9ab7-53ddec67d7ab"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-502520465B1105AF3FF7BF981A61753A"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)","Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, Biomedicine Group","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, Laboratory of Neurobiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Molecular Biology and Genetics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Annette","key":"burkhartannettepau","last":"Burkhart","locid":"7b6bd909-a011-463c-9e09-3623fee043b3","name":"Burkhart, Annette","orcid":"0000-0003-2086-4693","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tina","key":"skjørringetinapau","last":"Skjørringe","locid":"75e49845-8065-4dea-b009-24a75d84e69f","name":"Skjørringe, Tina","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kasper Bendix","key":"johnsenkasperbendixpau","last":"Johnsen","locid":"05baea19-a522-4d7d-9beb-95362028aec1","name":"Johnsen, Kasper Bendix","orcid":"0000-0002-1678-2436","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Piotr","key":"siupkapiotrpau","last":"Siupka","locid":"e7365196-e309-4349-af5f-058784335911","name":"Siupka, Piotr","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Louiza Bohn","key":"thomsenlouizabohnpau","last":"Thomsen","locid":"c4698d51-553a-4391-90b0-5379982b935f","name":"Thomsen, Louiza Bohn","orcid":"0000-0002-3144-7150","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Morten Schallburg","key":"nielsenmortenschallburgpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"556c3932-43bd-4042-9342-a3a65d6da37e","name":"Nielsen, Morten Schallburg","orcid":"0000-0001-9863-9694","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars Lykke","key":"thomsenlarslykkepau","last":"Thomsen","name":"Thomsen, Lars Lykke","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Torben","key":"moostorbenpau","last":"Moos","locid":"e51cbd29-97d2-42d8-bbca-11f026378a2f","name":"Moos, Torben","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26687231"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s12035-015-9582-7","issn":["08937648","15591182"],"issn_org":["08937648"],"issue":"10","journal":"Molecular Neurobiology","pages":"7237-7253","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Molecular Neurobiology","volume":"53"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84994754057"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-45f6c2cf-db97-42af-84f2-97d3ff6a2b88","au-d9686599-1e70-4a75-9ab7-53ddec67d7ab"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Expression of Iron-Related Proteins at the Neurovascular Unit Supports Reduction and Reoxidation of Iron for Transport Through the Blood-Brain Barrier","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-095.56-003425","year":2016,"yearsub":2016}
{"abstract":"A comparative analysis of the environmental and economic performance of seaweed production and biorefinery systems were modelled within the project MAB3 (www.mab3.dk). A framework for integrated sustainability modelling of the circular economy of offshore seaweed production and biorefinery systems using excess aquatic nutrients and atmospheric CO2 emissions as a resource for biobased production is proposed. The seaweed production system was pilot tested at two Danish coastal areas achieving relatively low productivities of 1 to 2 ton dry weight seaweed per hectare. Biorefinery systems producing ethanol and proteins (EP) or biogas and fertilizers (BF) as main products were compared. Results show that seaweed cultivation and biorefinery systems contributes to mitigation of climate change as well as water quality restoration. Improvements in the productivity (cultivation technology) and product portfolio (processing and cascade utilization) are needed for a seaweed biorefinery industry to become economically viable. The break-even point for the MAB3 EP biorefinery system is obtained by an increase in the seaweed productivity of a factor 2 to 4. Development of seaweed cultivation technology is ongoing and requires expanding the scale of production. Regarding the product portfolio, especially use of seaweed for pharmaceuticals and cosmetics will increase the profitability of the seaweed utilization compared to use for energy, feed and fertilizers. There are not synergies between the economic and environmental performance of the modelled systems in all aspects. The revenue of the EP biorefinery system was higher than the revenue from BF system, while BF production delivered larger mitigation of climate change, i.e. GHG emission reductions. Mitigation of aquatic eutrophication was highest for the EP system. The welfare economic value of the services delivered by the seaweed cultivation and biorefinery systems ranges between 5 and 20% of the raw seaweed production costs.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Thomsen, Marianne","Seghetta, Michele","Bruhn, Annette","Dolmer, Per","Tørring, Ditte B.","Hasler, Berit"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-236136"],"event":{"end":"2016-06-24","place":"Copenhagen, dk","start":"2016-06-19","title":"22nd International Seaweed Symposium taking place in Copenhagen, Denmark, June 19 - 24, 2016","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Circular economy","Climate change mitigation","Economic feasibility","Ecosystem services","LCA","Life cycle assessment","Seaweed biorefinery","Seaweed cultivation","Sustainability assessment"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the circular economy of seaweed as nutrient management instrument for biobased production","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-236136","ids":["au-bb099837-8dfc-411d-9e2d-66f166e97ebd"],"keyword":["Ecosystem Services","LCA","Life Cycle Assessment","Sustainability assessment","break-even point","circular economy","climate change mitigation","economic feasibility","eutrophication mitigation","seaweed biorefinery","seaweed cultivation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-F9A1CF1445540B3956891F1ECD37CB44"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Environmental Science, Department of Environmental Science - Emission modeling & environmental geography"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marianne","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","locid":"92402c50-d634-4163-a3fa-198f30c806c5","name":"Thomsen, Marianne","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Michele","key":"seghettapau","last":"Seghetta","locid":"28d76a35-221b-425c-a1fa-4ecfe1d37930","name":"Seghetta, Michele","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Annette","key":"bruhnpau","last":"Bruhn","locid":"15559017-3036-4e04-968e-338a24d800ce","name":"Bruhn, Annette","orcid":"0000-0002-7940-1338","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Per","key":"dolmerpau","last":"Dolmer","name":"Dolmer, Per","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ditte B.","key":"tørringpau","last":"Tørring","name":"Tørring, Ditte B.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Berit","key":"haslerpau","last":"Hasler","locid":"63d231d4-5285-481a-abec-99c2aff93b73","name":"Hasler, Berit","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-bb099837-8dfc-411d-9e2d-66f166e97ebd"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"The circular economy of seaweed as nutrient management instrument for biobased production","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-236136","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"The aim of the study is to assess the efficacy of seaweed for circular nutrient management to reduce eutrophication levels in the aquatic environment. We performed a comparative Life Cycle Assessment (LCA) of two reference waste management systems treating seaweed as biowaste, i.e. landfill disposal and combustion, and an alternative scenario using the seaweed Saccharina latissima as a resource for biobased fertilizer production. Life Cycle Impact Assessment (LCIA) methods were improved by using a cradle-to-cradle approach, quantifying fate factors for nitrogen and phosphorus loss from fertilized agriculture to the aquatic environment. We also differentiated between nitrogen- and phosphorus-limited marine water to improve the traditional freshwater impact category, making this indicator suitable for decision support in relation to coastal water management schemes. Offshore cultivation of Saccharina latissima with an average productivity of 150 Mg/km2 in Danish waters in 2014 was applied to a cultivation scenario of 208 km2. The bioresource scenario performs better than conventional biowaste management systems, delivering a net reduction in aquatic eutrophication levels of 32.29 kg N eq. and 16.58 kg PO43 − eq. per Mg (dry weight) of seaweed, quantified by the ReCiPe and CML impact assessment methods, respectively. Seaweed cultivation, harvest and reuse of excess nutrients from the aquatic environment is a promising approach for sustainable resource cycling in a future regenerative economy that exploits manmade emissions as a resource for closed loop biobased production while significantly reducing eutrophication levels in 3 out of 7 Danish river basin districts. We obtained at least 10% bioextraction of phosphorus manmade emissions (10%, 89% and > 100%) and contributed significantly to local nitrogen reduction goals according to the Water Framework Directive (23%, 78% and > 100% of the target).","author_count":4,"contributors":["Seghetta, Michele","Tørring, Ditte","Bruhn, Annette","Thomsen, Marianne"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-241086"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Circular nutrient management","Ecosystem services","Eutrophication","LCA","Seaweed cultivation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"bioextraction potential of seaweed in denmark an instrument for circular nutrient management","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/99743706/Seghetta_et_al_2016a.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-241086","identifier":[{"id":"84966373447","type":"scopus"},{"id":"27152993","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-c3d4d6c7-de06-4e4f-b69b-bc0580cf9faa"],"keyword":["ECOSYSTEM SERVICES","LCA","circular nutrient management","eutrophication","seaweed cultivation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F9EEBAC5BC27F4AB26E9B5C03DB60EE2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/99743706/Seghetta_et_al_2016a.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Environmental Science, Department of Environmental Science - Emission modeling & environmental geography"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Michele","key":"seghettapau","last":"Seghetta","locid":"28d76a35-221b-425c-a1fa-4ecfe1d37930","name":"Seghetta, Michele","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ditte","key":"tørringpau","last":"Tørring","name":"Tørring, Ditte","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Annette","key":"bruhnpau","last":"Bruhn","locid":"15559017-3036-4e04-968e-338a24d800ce","name":"Bruhn, Annette","orcid":"0000-0002-7940-1338","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marianne","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","locid":"92402c50-d634-4163-a3fa-198f30c806c5","name":"Thomsen, Marianne","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["27152993"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.scitotenv.2016.04.010","issn":["00489697","18791026"],"issn_org":["00489697"],"journal":"Science of the Total Environment","pages":"513-529","publisher":"Elsevier BV","publisher_org":"Elsevier B.V.","status":"p","title":"Science of the Total Environment","volume":"563-564"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84966373447"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-c3d4d6c7-de06-4e4f-b69b-bc0580cf9faa"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Bioextraction potential of seaweed in Denmark – an instrument for circular nutrient management","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-241086","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"[Open access]Multiple myeloma (MM) is a plasma cell malignancy with a significant heritable basis. Genome-wide association studies have transformed our understanding of MM predisposition, but individual studies have had limited power to discover risk loci. Here we perform a meta-analysis of these GWAS, add a new GWAS and perform replication analyses resulting in 9,866 cases and 239,188 controls. We confirm all nine known risk loci and discover eight new loci at 6p22.3 (rs34229995, P=1.31 x 10(-8)), 6q21 (rs9372120, P=9.09 x 10(-15)), 7q36.1 (rs7781265, P=9.71 x 10(-9)), 8q24.21 (rs1948915, P=4.20 x 10(-11)), 9p21.3 (rs2811710, P=1.72 x 10(-13)), 10p12.1 (rs2790457, P=1.77 x 10(-8)), 16q23.1 (rs7193541, P=5.00 x 10(-12)) and 20q13.13 (rs6066835, P=1.36 x 10(-13)), which localize in or near to JARID2, ATG5, SMARCD3, CCAT1, CDKN2A, WAC, RFWD3 and PREX1. These findings provide additional support for a polygenic model of MM and insight into the biological basis of tumour development","author_count":62,"contributors":["Mitchell, Jonathan S","Li, Ni","Weinhold, Niels","Försti, Asta","Ali, Mina","van Duin, Mark","Thorleifsson, Gudmar","Johnson, David C","Chen, Bowang","Halvarsson, Britt-Marie","Gudbjartsson, Daniel F","Kuiper, Rowan","Stephens, Owen W","Bertsch, Uta","Broderick, Peter","Campo, Chiara","Einsele, Hermann","Gregory, Walter A","Gullberg, Urban","Henrion, Marc","Hillengass, Jens","Hoffmann, Per","Jackson, Graham H","Johnsson, Ellinor","Jöud, Magnus","Kristinsson, Sigurður Y","Lenhoff, Stig","Lenive, Oleg","Mellqvist, Ulf-Henrik","Migliorini, Gabriele","Nahi, Hareth","Nelander, Sven","Nickel, Jolanta","Nöthen, Markus M","Rafnar, Thorunn","Ross, Fiona M","da Silva Filho, Miguel Inacio","Swaminathan, Bhairavi","Thomsen, Hauke","Turesson, Ingemar","Vangsted, Annette Juul","Vogel, Ulla","Waage, Anders","Walker, Brian A","Wihlborg, Anna-Karin","Broyl, Annemiek","Davies, Faith E","Thorsteinsdottir, Unnur","Langer, Christian","Hansson, Markus","Kaiser, Martin","Sonneveld, Pieter","Stefansson, Kari","Morgan, Gareth J","Goldschmidt, Hartmut","Hemminki, Kari","Nilsson, Björn","Houlston, Richard S"],"cuid":["S02-098.30-768597"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"51-200 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Journal Article"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-WORK"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-WORK","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"genome wide association study identifies multiple susceptibility loci for multiple myeloma","src":["ku","nfa"],"src-code":["DI-GV-WORK","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/ncomms12050","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-098.30-768597","identifier":[{"id":"PMC4932178","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"27363682","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84977123396","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-02c072ba-a4b8-4f90-9f45-11bad0abe1c4","nfa-5d3edf03-1528-4a87-bd87-8889f5518ca9"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-1236030541B9A9610EDACCB51661FBAB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/ncomms12050","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"nfa national research centre for the worki