{"abstract":"In vitro blood-brain barrier (BBB) models based on primary brain endothelial cells (BECs) cultured as monoculture or in co-culture with primary astrocytes and pericytes are useful for studying many properties of the BBB. The BECs retain their expression of tight junction proteins and efflux transporters leading to high trans-endothelial electric resistance (TEER) and low passive paracellular permeability. The BECs, astrocytes and pericytes are often isolated from small rodents. Larger species as cows and pigs however, reveal a higher yield, are readily available and have a closer resemblance to humans, which make them favorable high-throughput sources for cellular isolation. The aim of the present study has been to determine if the preferable combination of purely porcine cells isolated from the 6 months old domestic pigs, i.e. porcine brain endothelial cells (PBECs) in co-culture with porcine astrocytes and pericytes, would compare with PBECs co-cultured with astrocytes and pericytes isolated from newborn rats with respect to TEER value and low passive permeability. The astrocytes and pericytes were grown both as contact and non-contact co-cultures as well as in triple culture to examine their effects on the PBECs for barrier formation as revealed by TEER, passive permeability, and expression patterns of tight junction proteins, efflux transporters and the transferrin receptor. This syngenic porcine in vitro BBB model is comparable to triple cultures using PBECs, rat astrocytes and rat pericytes with respect to TEER formation, low passive permeability, and expression of hallmark proteins signifying the brain endothelium (tight junction proteins claudin 5 and occludin, the efflux transporters P-glycoprotein (PgP) and breast cancer related protein (BCRP), and the transferrin receptor).","author_count":3,"contributors":["Thomsen, Louiza Bohn","Burkhart, Annette","Moos, Torben"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-099403"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a triple culture model of the blood brain barrier using porcine brain endothelial cells astrocytes and pericytes","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0134765","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-099403","identifier":[{"id":"84941992267","type":"scopus"},{"id":"26241648","type":"pmid"},{"id":"WOS:000358942700065","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-aa1f39ce-ff0e-4e58-a61a-c6882b29e755"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7B973069D7F73AABB6DEF390E60A68EF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0134765","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/217456206/journal.pone.0134765.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, Biomedicine Group","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, Laboratory of Neurobiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Louiza Bohn","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","locid":"c4698d51-553a-4391-90b0-5379982b935f","name":"Thomsen, Louiza Bohn","orcid":"0000-0002-3144-7150","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Annette","key":"burkhartpau","last":"Burkhart","locid":"7b6bd909-a011-463c-9e09-3623fee043b3","name":"Burkhart, Annette","orcid":"0000-0003-2086-4693","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Torben","key":"moospau","last":"Moos","locid":"e51cbd29-97d2-42d8-bbca-11f026378a2f","name":"Moos, Torben","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26241648"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1371/journal.pone.0134765","issn":["19326203"],"issue":"8","journal":"PLOS ONE","paperid":"e0134765","publisher":"Public Library of Science","status":"p","title":"PLOS ONE","volume":"10"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84941992267"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-aa1f39ce-ff0e-4e58-a61a-c6882b29e755"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"A triple culture model of the blood-brain barrier using porcine brain endothelial cells, astrocytes and pericytes","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-099403","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Primary brain capillary endothelial cells (BCECs) are a promising tool to study the blood-brain barrier (BBB) in vitro, as they maintain many important characteristics of the BBB in vivo, especially when co-cultured with pericytes and/or astrocytes. A novel strategy for drug delivery to the brain is to transform BCECs into protein factories by genetic modifications leading to secretion of otherwise BBB impermeable proteins into the central nervous system. However, a huge challenge underlying this strategy is to enable transfection of non-mitotic BCECs, taking a non-viral approach. We therefore aimed to study transfection in primary, non-mitotic BCECs cultured with defined BBB properties without disrupting the cells' integrity. METHODS: Primary cultures of BCECs, pericytes and astrocytes were generated from rat brains and used in three different in vitro BBB experimental arrangements, which were characterised based on a their expression of tight junction proteins and other BBB specific proteins, high trans-endothelial electrical resistance (TEER), and low passive permeability to radiolabeled mannitol. Recombinant gene expression and protein synthesis were examined in primary BCECs. The BCECs were transfected using a commercially available transfection agent Turbofect™ to express the red fluorescent protein HcRed1-C1. The BCECs were transfected at different time points to monitor transfection in relation to mitotic or non-mitotic cells, as indicated by fluorescence-activated cell sorting analysis after 5-and 6-carboxylfluorescein diacetate succinidyl ester incorporation. RESULTS: The cell cultures exhibited important BBB characteristics judged from their expression of BBB specific proteins, high TEER values, and low passive permeability. Among the three in vitro BBB models, co-culturing with BCECs and astrocytes was well suited for the transfection studies. Transfection was independent of cell division and with equal efficacy between the mitotic and non-mitotic BCECs. Importantly, transfection of BCECs exhibiting BBB characteristics did not alter the integrity of the BCECs cell layer. CONCLUSIONS: The data clearly indicate that non-viral gene therapy of BCECs is possible in primary culture conditions with an intact BBB.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Burkhart, Annette","Thomsen, Louiza Bohn","Thomsen, Maj Schneider","Lichota, Jacek","Fazakas, Csilla","Krizbai, István","Moos, Torben"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-113536"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"transfection of brain capillary endothelial cells in primary culture with defined blood brain barrier properties","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12987-015-0015-9","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-113536","identifier":[{"id":"WOS:000210115700001","type":"wos"},{"id":"84938570940","type":"scopus"},{"id":"26246240","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-da8245cb-d6b5-41ca-838b-3ae6448a6c59"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-237A21FDB515DFEEEE28105AEA093D2E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12987-015-0015-9","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/217372991/s12987_015_0015_9.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, Biomedicine Group","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, Laboratory of Neurobiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Annette Burkhart","key":"burkhartannettepau","last":"Larsen","locid":"7b6bd909-a011-463c-9e09-3623fee043b3","name":"Burkhart, Annette","name_org":"Larsen, Annette Burkhart","orcid":"0000-0003-2086-4693","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Louiza Bohn","key":"thomsenlouizabohnpau","last":"Thomsen","locid":"c4698d51-553a-4391-90b0-5379982b935f","name":"Thomsen, Louiza Bohn","orcid":"0000-0002-3144-7150","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Maj Schneider","key":"thomsenmajschneiderpau","last":"Thomsen","locid":"500ff43a-765e-4d61-9bbd-f228196ed49d","name":"Thomsen, Maj Schneider","orcid":"0000-0002-8385-7039","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jacek","key":"lichotajacekpau","last":"Lichota","locid":"56885af4-f202-4e65-9e09-8262504b7313","name":"Lichota, Jacek","orcid":"0000-0002-9943-5201","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Csilla","key":"fazakascsillapau","last":"Fazakas","name":"Fazakas, Csilla","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"István","key":"krizbaiistvánpau","last":"Krizbai","name":"Krizbai, István","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Torben","key":"moostorbenpau","last":"Moos","locid":"e51cbd29-97d2-42d8-bbca-11f026378a2f","name":"Moos, Torben","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26246240"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s12987-015-0015-9","issn":["20458118"],"issue":"1","journal":"Fluids and Barriers of the CNS","paperid":"19","publisher":"BioMed Central","status":"p","title":"Fluids and Barriers of the CNS","volume":"12"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84938570940"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-da8245cb-d6b5-41ca-838b-3ae6448a6c59"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Transfection of brain capillary endothelial cells in primary culture with defined blood-brain barrier properties","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-113536","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Background: The potential for treatment of chronic disorders affecting the CNS is complicated by the inability of several drugs to cross the blood-brain barrier (BBB). None-viral gene therapy applied to brain capillary endothelial cells (BCECs) denotes a novel approach to overcome the restraints in this passage, as turning BCECs into recombinant protein factories by transfection could result in protein secretion into the brain. Aim: The aim of the present study was to investigate the possibility of transfection to primary rat brain capillary endothelial cells (RBEC) for recombinant protein synthesis. Results: mRNA expression of proteins with neuroprotective potential in RBEC were enabled. Their expression patters were compared with those of RBE4 and HeLa cells using RT-qPCR analyzes. The evidence for protein synthesis and secretion was obtained by detection of FLAG-tagged to the C-terminal of any of the proteins. Morphological examination of the protein expression was determined using immunofluorescence detecting FLAG. Additionally, the transfection efficiency were determined by Flow cytometry. Perspective: Our study opens for knowledge on how non-viral gene therapy to BCECs can lead to protein secretion with the perspective of enabling therapeutic protein to target neurons inside the CNS otherwise inhibited to access due to the restraints of the BBB. This therapeutic strategy could be beneficial in treatment of inherited diseases and classical neurodegenerative disorders.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Burkhart, Annette","Thomsen, Louiza Bohn","Moos, Torben"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-081523"],"event":{"end":"2014-06-20","place":"New London, NH, us","start":"2014-06-15","title":"Barriers of the CNS -","year":"2014"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"gene delivery of therapeutic polypeptides to brain capillary endothelial cells for protein secretion","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-081523","ids":["aau-6c2ebab3-54ef-4608-bfe3-a8f0b36c55c0"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-D0C8B350ACF843144E6C923319926136"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, Biomedicine Group","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, Laboratory of Neurobiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Annette Burkhart","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"7b6bd909-a011-463c-9e09-3623fee043b3","name":"Burkhart, Annette","name_org":"Larsen, Annette Burkhart","orcid":"0000-0003-2086-4693","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Louiza Bohn","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","locid":"c4698d51-553a-4391-90b0-5379982b935f","name":"Thomsen, Louiza Bohn","orcid":"0000-0002-3144-7150","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Torben","key":"moospau","last":"Moos","locid":"e51cbd29-97d2-42d8-bbca-11f026378a2f","name":"Moos, Torben","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-6c2ebab3-54ef-4608-bfe3-a8f0b36c55c0"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Gene delivery of therapeutic polypeptides to brain capillary endothelial cells for protein secretion","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-081523","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
