tal, Klinik Hoved-Orto"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Cathrine Wildenschild","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"d88e4194-e5bc-4076-9a02-8b70b5bc0597","name":"Nielsen, Cathrine Wildenschild","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Cathrine","key":"wildenschildpau","last":"Wildenschild","name":"Wildenschild, Cathrine","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Frank","key":"mehnertpau","last":"Mehnert","locid":"05507c2f-1643-4e1f-9a10-664bd8eeed1d","name":"Mehnert, Frank","orcid":"0000-0001-7639-7356","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"RW","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","locid":"36e7af2c-e02f-48d4-b124-0f1bd95b1748","name":"Thomsen, Reimar Wernich","name_org":"Thomsen, RW","orcid":"0000-0001-9135-3474","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","first":"Helle Klingenberg","key":"iversenpau","last":"Iversen","locid":"02552302-5333-48e0-acde-b9a821eab783","name":"Iversen, Helle Klingenberg","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Karsten","key":"vestergaardpau","last":"Vestergaard","locid":"f7829ff6-1de7-4d20-9f56-71f1848b8a4c","name":"Vestergaard, Karsten","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Annette","key":"ingemanpau","last":"Ingeman","locid":"1d452ffc-d24a-47ab-afdd-cf45adfd9502","name":"Ingeman, Annette","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Paaske","key":"johnsenpau","last":"Johnsen","locid":"4664f7a0-39e7-4f46-9121-1c3999eb3d09","name":"Johnsen, Søren Paaske","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["24399886"],"pub":{"doi":"10.2147/clep.s50449","issn":["11791349"],"journal":"Clinical Epidemiology","pages":"27-36","publisher":"Dove Medical Press Ltd","publisher_org":"Dove Medical Press Ltd.","status":"p","title":"Clinical Epidemiology","volume":"6"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84891478560"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-fe90af75-ad16-49ae-a089-e4539105f2a5","au-aa14bd74-7357-4449-bc31-30e2cdace709","ku-08078920-e097-4657-89b2-c85dcba0e83f","ku-ad25f0a2-8d9d-42ce-b22e-b397f4ad1d6f"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Registration of acute stroke: validity in the Danish Stroke Registry and the Danish National Registry of Patients","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S04-095.50-012108","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"This article is an introduction to how architecture’s context and conditions can be understood as signaletic with reference to Gilles Deleuze’s concept of the signaletic material. The understanding of architecture’s signaletic material addresses the process of becoming through the potentials of context and the requests towards function and programme, as well as through the methods for creating architecture - all seen as conditional components of a specific work of architecture and, consequently, as part of the signaletic material. A visit to the New Acropolis Museum is analysed to discuss how the potential of the in-between encounters of architecture, context and the experiencing subject can be part of the signaletic material and the process of becoming. This potential is actualised, for instance, in relation to the movement through the museum. The museum architecture affords experiences on potentially several levels spanning from the most pragmatic and functional use of the building as exhibition space, restaurant, book shop, etc. to the awareness of being part of an architectural intentionality as a moving body, a contemplating viewer and as a perceiver of relations between the museum building and its historical and geographical context. In the article the term ‘‘visitor’’ is used to emphasise this complexity of experiential potential that is made accessible by the museum’s architectural design.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Jakobsen, Annette Svaneklink"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-125736"],"filters":{"added":"2023-01","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-ART"],"level3":{"ART":["DI-ART-AAA","DI-ART-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-ART-AAA"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"experience in between architecture and context the new acropolis museum athens","src":["arka"],"src-code":["DI-ART-AAA"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://adk.elsevierpure.com/ws/files/35995543/18158_63927_1_PB.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-125736","identifier":[{"id":"84868136471","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["arka-ed73bff7-957f-4e28-af23-9fb144d5c215"],"keyword":["No"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-A8C19A19923ABA8AD566057AA667144A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.aestheticsandculture.net/index.php/jac/article/view/18158","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://adk.elsevierpure.com/ws/files/35995543/18158_63927_1_PB.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aarhus school of architecture","l2":"DI-ART","l2n":"Artistic Higher Education Institutions","l3":"DI-ART-AAA","l3nn":"Aarhus School of Architecture","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Aarhus School of Architecture","namevar":["Aarhus School of Architecture","Aarhus School of Architecture, The theory and history of architecture"],"nora_code":"DI-ART-AAA","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Annette Svaneklink","key":"jakobsenpau","last":"Jakobsen","locid":"e41aa4a8-104e-4152-8152-a91f2a727332","name":"Jakobsen, Annette Svaneklink","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Bodil Marie Stavning","key":"thomsenpedh","last":"Thomsen","name":"Thomsen, Bodil Marie Stavning","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"John","key":"sundholmpedh","last":"Sundholm","name":"Sundholm, John","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Ulla Angkjær","key":"jørgensenpedh","last":"Jørgensen","name":"Jørgensen, Ulla Angkjær","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["eISSN 20004214"],"place":"Stockholm, Sweden","status":"p","subtitle":"From Sign to Signal","title":"Journal of Aesthetics &amp; Culture","volume":"vol.4"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Artistic Higher Education Institutions","All Danish Affiliations","Artistic Higher Education Institutions","DI-ALL","DI-ART","DI-ART-ALL"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["arka-ed73bff7-957f-4e28-af23-9fb144d5c215"],"src":["Aarhus School of Architecture"],"title":"Experience in-between architecture and context: the New Acropolis Museum, Athens","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-125736","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"The objectives of this study were to develop and test a system for automatic washing of the hooves of dairy cows and to evaluate the effect of frequent automatic washing on the prevalence of digital dermatitis (DD). An automatic hoof washer was developed in an experimental dairy herd and tested in 6 commercial dairy herds in 2 experiments (1 and 2). In the experimental herd, automatic hoof washing resulted in cleaner hooves. In experiments 1 and 2, cows were washed after each milking on the left side only, leaving the right side unwashed as a within-cow control. In experiment 1, hooves were washed with a water and 0.4% soap solution. In experiment 2, hooves were washed with water only. In each experiment, DD was scored in a hoof-trimming chute approximately 60 d after the start of hoof washing. Data were analyzed using a generalized linear mixed model. The outcome was the DD status of each leg (DD positive or DD negative). Herd and cow within herd were included as random effects, and treatment (washing or control) was included as a fixed effect. The statistical analyses showed that the odds ratio of having DD was 1.48 in the control leg compared with the washed leg in experiment 1. In experiment 2, the odds ratio of having DD was 1.27 in the control leg compared with the washed leg. We concluded that automatic washing of hooves with water and soap can help decrease the prevalence of DD in commercial dairy herds.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Thomsen, Peter T.","Kjær Ersbøll, Annette","Sørensen, Jan Tind"],"cuid":["S02-091.60-021354"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"short communication automatic washing of hooves can help control digital dermatitis in dairy cows","src":["au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3168/jds.2011-5171","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-091.60-021354","identifier":[{"id":"84869489802","type":"scopus"},{"id":"23063150","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-76e4d80e-869b-4e17-ad1c-5c2f2878f4a1","sdu-87e0af8b-0d45-4cd5-bb0c-774aa139dc97"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-783ACD758D51A65F16BF3FA5177C0BA7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3168/jds.2011-5171","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Animal and Veterinary Sciences, Department of Animal and Veterinary Sciences - ANIS Welfare"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, National Institute of Public Health, Department of Population Health and Morbidity","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, National Institute of Public Health, Research Programme on Health and Morbidity in Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter Thorup","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","locid":"3ebc7472-4ef2-4198-8d2e-f8a39f82c114","name":"Thomsen, Peter T.","name_org":"Thomsen, Peter Thorup","orcid":"0000-0002-0896-1610","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Annette Kjær","key":"ersbøllpau","last":"Ersbøll","locid":"ba343517-a6c5-47c1-a8ba-4cbe00b7409c","name":"Ersbøll, Annette Kjær","orcid":"0000-0002-9407-3387","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jan Tind","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"a81162cd-d4bf-46b7-82b8-89e1fe974b22","name":"Sørensen, Jan Tind","orcid":"0000-0002-5915-1474","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["23063150"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3168/jds.2011-5171","issn":["00220302","15253198"],"issn_org":["00220302"],"issue":"12","journal":"Journal of Dairy Science","pages":"7195-7199","publisher":"Elsevier Inc.","status":"p","title":"Journal of Dairy Science","volume":"95"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84869489802"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-76e4d80e-869b-4e17-ad1c-5c2f2878f4a1","sdu-87e0af8b-0d45-4cd5-bb0c-774aa139dc97"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Short communication : Automatic washing of hooves can help control digital dermatitis in dairy cows","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-091.60-021354","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"The Nordic countries Denmark (DK), Finland (FIN), Norway (NO) and Sweden (SE) all have unique national databases holding the disease records of dairy cows. The objective of this study was to estimate and compare completeness for locomotor disorders in the four Nordic national databases. Completeness figures for farmer-recorded disease events were calculated on two different levels: the first refers to disease events that were observed on the farm regardless of whether a veterinarian had been involved (FARMER); the second refers to farmer records of cases attended by a veterinarian, i.e. to veterinarian-treated disease events (VET). A sample of herds with 15 or more cows was obtained from a simple random sample of dairy farms in FIN, NO and SE, and from a systematic random sample in OK. There were 105, 167, 179 and 129 participating farmers in DK, FIN, NO and SE, respectively, and during two 2-month periods in 2008 these farmers recorded the disease events they observed on the farm. Data from the four national databases were extracted in May 2009. The two data sources, farmer recordings and national databases, were managed in a comparable way in all four countries, and common diagnostic codes were created and added to match recordings appearing in both datasets. In all 555 farmers completed data records in the first data-recording period, and 515 farmers did so in the second period. In DK, FIN, NO and SE, 55%, 77%, 82% and 75%, participating farmers completed the recordings during the first recording period, respectively; the corresponding figures for the second recording period were 71%, 82%, 83% and 91%. To calculate completeness, disease cases recorded in the national databases were compared with the farmer recordings using an exact match for the locomotor complex defined as same country, herd identification number (id), cow id, and event date at the levels of FARMER and VET. Completeness at FARMER level were 0.22, 0.21, 0.23 and 0.12 in DK, FIN, NO and SE, respectively. At VET level they were 0.37, 0.27, 0.34 and 0.17. To compare differences in completeness between countries exact 95% confidence intervals were calculated. There were significant differences in completeness between DK and SE at both FARMER and VET level. The completeness indicate that the ability to estimate true disease occurrences in the four national databases varies and is in general poor. Completeness should be taken into account when disease occurrences in different countries are compared. (C) 2012 Elsevier B.V. All rights reserved.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Lind, Ann-Kristina","Thomsen, Peter T.","Ersbøll, Annette Kjær","Espetvedt, Mari","Wolff, Cecilia","Rintakoski, Simo","Houe, Hans"],"cuid":["S03-098.12-022219"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Finland","Norway","Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Norwegian University of Life Sciences","Swedish University of Agricultural Sciences","University of Helsinki"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"validation of nordic dairy cattle disease recording databases completeness for locomotor disorders","src":["au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/100713219/1_s2.0_S0167587712002097_main.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S03-098.12-022219","identifier":[{"id":"84868214688","type":"scopus"},{"id":"22819636","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-82b8e3fd-d9cf-4cb8-8750-79db124e721e","ku-18afdebf-4f30-4941-bbeb-d86d6b6d462b","sdu-0b6c0e51-2071-4